    },
    {
      "id": "1e9931162300104c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "Inputs and outputs are the same as for [master key providers](./master-key-provider-interface.md). A master key MUST supply itself and MUST NOT supply any other master keys.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "92063092bd61a729",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "Inputs and outputs are the same as for [master key providers](./master-key-provider-interface.md). A master key MUST supply itself and MUST NOT supply any other master keys.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0de17ba61f4bf32f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "Inputs and outputs are the same as for [master key providers](./master-key-provider-interface.md). A master key SHOULD attempt to decrypt a data key using itself. A master key MUST not attempt to use any other master keys.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-data-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7e079b367a1265ba",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "This interface is used to generate and encrypt a data key. The master key MUST generate a data key and MUST then encrypt that data key. Inputs to this interface MUST include the algorithm suite and the encryption context. The output of this interface MUST include the plaintext data key, the data key encrypted under the master key, and information that can identify which master key was used to generate and encrypt the data key. If the master key cannot generate or encrypt the data key, the call MUST result in an error.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "generate-data-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5487af7abeb9240b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "This interface is used to encrypt a data key. The master key MUST encrypt the data key. Inputs to this interface MUST include the algorithm suite, the encryption context, the encrypted data key, and information that can identify which master key was used to encrypt the data key. The output of this interface MUST include a value that this master key can use to obtain the plaintext data key. Most commonly, this will be the result of an encryption operation. If the master key cannot encrypt the data key, the call MUST result in an error.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "encrypt-data-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ebb9fdb381882058",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "This is a legacy specification. Master key providers SHOULD NOT be included in any additional implementations. Any new implementations MUST include [Keyrings](./keyring-interface.md) instead.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-provider-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "legacy",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7eb458c38459ea52",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "This specification defines the common behavior between the two implementations that determine the REQUIRED functionality.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-provider-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "consistency",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fd0dc5fef997ec14",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "- Provider ID: A value that identifies a master key provider. This concept is equivalent to \"key namespace\" for Keyrings. - Key ID: A value that identifies a master key within the context of a master key provider. This concept is equivalent to \"key name\" for Keyrings. - Provider Info: The value that is written to a serialized encrypted data key that identifies a master key within the context of a master key provider. This MUST always be equal to the master key's key ID with the exception of the raw AES master key. For a detailed description of this exception, see the [Raw AES Keyring specification](./raw-aes-keyring.md).",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-provider-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "terms",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "36019b825514e0ef",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "This interface provides a way for a master key provider to return master keys. An implementation MUST support master key selection by key ID. An implementation MAY support master key selection by provider info or provider ID. The output of this interface MUST be a master key. If the master key provider cannot locate an appropriate master key, the call MUST result in an error.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-provider-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dbee223a7373795a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "This interface provides a way for a master key provider to indicate which master keys SHOULD be used for encryption. Inputs to this interface MUST include the encryption context. Inputs MAY include the plaintext body and plaintext size. The output of this interface MUST include a list of all master keys that SHOULD be used for encryption. The output of this interface MUST indicate which one of those master keys MUST be used to generate the data key.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-provider-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "30a340f0b6a45dd2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "This interface is used to decrypt a data key. The master key provider SHOULD attempt to decrypt the data key by passing the request to any master keys that it has access to until it has either exhausted available master keys or obtained a plaintext data key. Inputs to this interface MUST include the algorithm suite, the encryption context, and a list of encrypted data keys. The output of this interface MUST include the decrypted data key and information that can identify which master key decrypted the data key. If the master key provider cannot decrypt the data key, the call MUST result in an error.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/master-key-provider-interface.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-data-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8133033b39895ddb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2,
      "quote": "While these structures will usually be represented as objects, lower level languages MAY represent these fields in a less strictly defined way as long as all field properties are still upheld.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "overview",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ba0a73f2b726de36",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 7,
      "quote": "This specification uses the terms \"encrypt\" and \"decrypt\" for simplicity, but the actual process by which a key provider obtains the plaintext data key from the ciphertext and vice versa MAY be any reversible operation, though we expect that most will use encryption.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "structure",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ebdf848d000a851",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "Some key provider MUST be capable of deterministically obtaining the plaintext key from the ciphertext.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "ciphertext",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8450d76a16429f6a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "Users SHOULD use the encryption context to store: - Non-secret data that MUST remain associated with the [message](../data-format/message.md) ciphertext. - Data that is useful in logging and tracking, such as data about the file type, purpose, or ownership. Users MUST NOT use the encryption context to store secret data.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "structure-1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c9acf485ab94cf89",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "The [ciphertext](#ciphertext) of each encrypted data key in this list MUST be an opaque form of the plaintext data key from this set of encryption materials.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "encrypted-data-keys",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2b7a848d40b3e387",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "The plaintext data key SHOULD be stored as immutable data.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "plaintext-data-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4a27281f57c677a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "The plaintext data key SHOULD offer an interface to zero the plaintext data key.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "plaintext-data-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "14b5012bd8828218",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "The value of this key MUST be kept secret.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "signing-key",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "163f04f19aba478e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "The plaintext data key SHOULD be stored as immutable data.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/structures.md",
      "target_section": "plaintext-data-key-1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9c587e4572a10bfc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "The plaintext data key SHOULD offer an interface to zero the plaintext data key.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/compliance_exceptions/structures.txt",
