      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e41fc0e32e37fdb2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 326,
      "quote": "On initialization of the local CMC, the caller MUST provide the following: - [Entry Capacity](#entry-capacity) The local CMC MUST also define the following: - [Entry Pruning Tail Size](#entry-pruning-tail-size)",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "initialization",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c45712efd3365caf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 385,
      "quote": "After a cache entry's TTL has elapsed, we say that the entry is _TTL-expired_, and a CMC MUST NOT return the entry to any caller.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "time-to-live-ttl",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6af4885425710161",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 390,
      "quote": "The CMC MUST validate that the cache entry has not exceeded it's stored [TTL](#time-to-live-ttl).",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "get-cache-entry",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cb631a926ba507a3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 394,
      "quote": "The local CMC MUST NOT return any TTL-expired entry.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "get-cache-entry",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cc523be5bbd842ca",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 407,
      "quote": "When performing a Get Cache Entry operation, the local CMC MUST [prune TTL-expired cache entries](#pruning).",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "get-cache-entry",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef4f9b807c1fe4fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 448,
      "quote": "However, before returning the local CMC MUST evict least-recently used entries until the number of stored entries does not exceed the entry capacity.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "put-cache-entry",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "af03b4558307c009",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 455,
      "quote": "The local CMC MUST NOT store more entries than this value, except temporarily while performing a Put Cache Entry operation.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "entry-capacity",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8b35cbd72feec6cf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 480,
      "quote": "While performing a Put Cache Entry operation, the local CMC MAY store more entries than the entry capacity.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "put-cache-entry",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cc5cbb84f4f1ffca",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 575,
      "quote": "Updating usage metadata SHOULD be atomic.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "usage-metadata",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "455c44e11f377ba6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 591,
      "quote": "The local CMC SHOULD also periodically evict all TTL-expired entries among the `N` least recently used entries.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "pruning",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "793b43cb2c98e13a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 605,
      "quote": "To prune TTL-expired cache entries, the local CMC MUST evict all TTL-expired entries among the `N` least recently used entries, where `N` is the [Entry Pruning Tail Size](#entry-pruning-tail-size).",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMCs/LocalCMC.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "pruning",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bc8c93c413f46840",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "The CMM MUST validate the [Encryption Context](structures.md#encryption-context) by comparing it to the customer supplied [Reproduced Encryption Context](structures.md#encryption-context) in [decrypt materials request](#decrypt-materials-request). For every key that exists in both [Reproduced Encryption Context](structures.md#encryption-context) and [Encryption Context](structures.md#encryption-context), the values MUST be equal or the operation MUST fail.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-materials",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4016f9290af4a605",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "- All key-value pairs that exist in [Reproduced Encryption Context](structures.md#encryption-context) but do not exist in encryption context on the [decrypt materials request](#decrypt-materials-request) SHOULD be appended to the decryption materials.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-materials",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cc808e6ddc2b6c21",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "On default CMM initialization, the caller MUST provide the following value: - [Keyring](#keyring)",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "initialization",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "13d438a987f20e90",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "When the CMM gets an [encryption materials request](#encryption-materials-request), it MUST return [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) appropriate for the request.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "46a9a09680fe4099",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "- Every encrypted data key in this list MUST correspond to the above plaintext data key.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f75178ca2bcc329",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "The encryption materials returned MUST include the following:",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dec5a6fcb34fa9ff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "The CMM MUST ensure that the encryption materials returned are valid. - The encryption materials returned MUST follow the specification for [encryption-materials](structures.md#encryption-materials). - The value of the plaintext data key MUST be non-NULL. - The plaintext data key length MUST be equal to the [key derivation input length](algorithm-suites.md#key-derivation-input-length). - The encrypted data keys list MUST contain at least one encrypted data key. - If the algorithm suite contains a signing algorithm, the encryption materials returned MUST include the generated signing key. - For every key in [Required Encryption Context Keys](structures.md#required-encryption-context-keys) there MUST be a matching key in the [Encryption Context](structures.md#encryption-context-1).",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "598a201c6c4434a8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "- The [Required Encryption Context Keys](structures.md#required-encryption-context-keys) MUST be a super set of the Required Encryption Context Keys in the [encryption materials request](#encryption-materials-request).",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d9961ce22d6e91a7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "If the algorithm suite contains a [signing algorithm](algorithm-suites.md#signature-algorithm): - The CMM MUST include a [signing key](structures.md#signing-key). - The CMM SHOULD also add a key-value pair using the reserved key `aws-crypto-public-key` to the encryption context. If it does, the mapped value SHOULD be the signature verification key corresponding to the signing key. If the algorithm suite does not contain a [signing algorithm](algorithm-suites.md#signature-algorithm): - The CMM SHOULD NOT add a key-value pair using the reserved key `aws-crypto-public-key` to the encryption context.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0f699f035c33f9f6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "- The CMM MAY modify the encryption context.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5a2981070de52ef3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "If the algorithm suite contains a [signing algorithm](algorithm-suites.md#signature-algorithm), the default CMM MUST Add the key-value pair of key `aws-crypto-public-key`, value `base64-encoded public verification key` to the [encryption context](structures.md#encryption-context).",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fe9a2f237260f1ca",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "If the algorithm suite contains a [signing algorithm](algorithm-suites.md#signature-algorithm), the default CMM MUST Generate a [signing key](structures.md#signing-key).",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e1ea3855d1458427",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "If the encryption context included in the [encryption materials request](cmm-interface.md#encryption-materials-request) already contains the `aws-crypto-public-key` key, this operation MUST fail rather than overwrite the associated value.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8fc20ecd5453532",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "- If the encryption materials request contains an algorithm suite, the encryption materials returned SHOULD contain the same algorithm suite.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d0be2f8386a45a3f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "- If the [encryption materials request](cmm-interface.md#encryption- materials-request) does contain an algorithm suite, the encryption materials returned MUST contain the same algorithm suite.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3f3c90bdcdd80dcf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 192,
      "quote": "- If the [encryption materials request](cmm-interface.md#encryption- materials-request) does not contain an algorithm suite, the operation MUST add the default algorithm suite for the [commitment policy](./commitment-policy.md#supported-commitment-policy-enum) as the algorithm suite in the encryption materials returned.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "400402ee1cf5ba1c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 207,
      "quote": "On each call to Get Encryption Materials, the default CMM MUST make a call to its [keyring's](#keyring) [On Encrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt) operation.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8791916a013aa79",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 213,
      "quote": "The default CMM MUST obtain the Plaintext Data Key from the On Encrypt Response and include it in the [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) returned.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "86f4b36c0f49aa3b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 220,
      "quote": "The default CMM MUST obtain the [Encrypted Data Keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-keys) from the On Encrypt Response and include it in the [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) returned.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5aaad8e37baced0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 229,
      "quote": "- If the [encryption materials request](cmm-interface.md#encryption- materials-request) does contain an algorithm suite, the request MUST fail if the algorithm suite is not supported by the [commitment policy](./commitment-policy.md#supported-commitment-policy-enum) on the request.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "336f3f939a1e26b0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 276,
      "quote": "Adding the key `aws-crypto-public-key` SHOULD be done to a copy of the encryption context so that the caller's encryption context is not mutated.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/default-cmm.md",
      "target_section": "get-encryption-materials",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "893097a8c172cd9e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 315,
      "quote": "When the CMM gets a [decrypt materials request](#decrypt-materials-request), it MUST return [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) appropriate for the request.",
      "source": "AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/dafny/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/src/CMMs/DefaultCMM.dfy",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/cmm-interface.md",
