      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface/overview.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface.md",
      "target_section": "overview",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Keyring implementations SHOULD provide integrity guarantees for the [encrypted data keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-key)\nthey return on [OnEncrypt](#onencrypt) such that tampered versions of those encrypted data keys,\nif input into [OnDecrypt](#ondecrypt), are overwhelmingly likely to cause a decryption failure\n(i.e.\n",
      "id": "b9d4c3910aa6b78f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "Keyring implementations SHOULD provide integrity guarantees for the [encrypted data keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-key) they return on [OnEncrypt](#onencrypt) such that tampered versions of those encrypted data keys, if input into [OnDecrypt](#ondecrypt), are overwhelmingly likely to cause a decryption failure (i.e.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface/security-considerations.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface.md",
      "target_section": "security-considerations",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Such integrity guarantees SHOULD include the integrity of the [encryption context](structures.md#encryption-context)\nsuch that, if the encryption context used as input to OnEncrypt to produce an encrypted data key is\ndifferent than the encryption context input to OnDecrypt to decrypt that encrypted data key,\nthe decryption is overwhelmingly likely to fail.\n",
      "id": "181411a01f64a71b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Such integrity guarantees SHOULD include the integrity of the [encryption context](structures.md#encryption-context) such that, if the encryption context used as input to OnEncrypt to produce an encrypted data key is different than the encryption context input to OnDecrypt to decrypt that encrypted data key, the decryption is overwhelmingly likely to fail.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface/security-considerations.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface.md",
      "target_section": "security-considerations",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Users SHOULD use a keyring that protects wrapping keys and performs cryptographic operations within a secure boundary.\n",
      "id": "aadc2796001adc03",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Users SHOULD use a keyring that protects wrapping keys and performs cryptographic operations within a secure boundary.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface/security-considerations.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface.md",
      "target_section": "security-considerations",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The [raw AES keyring](raw-aes-keyring.md) and [raw RSA keyring](raw-rsa-keyring.md) MAY be used,\nhowever users should refer to their specification for notes on their respective security considerations.\n",
      "id": "89fd57fe69751912",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "The [raw AES keyring](raw-aes-keyring.md) and [raw RSA keyring](raw-rsa-keyring.md) MAY be used, however users should refer to their specification for notes on their respective security considerations.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface/security-considerations.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface.md",
      "target_section": "security-considerations",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Due to this simplified architecture, master keys and master key providers are going to be deprecated in the future,\nand new implementations SHOULD use keyrings.\n",
      "id": "c22b67c15b5a29c2",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "Due to this simplified architecture, master keys and master key providers are going to be deprecated in the future, and new implementations SHOULD use keyrings.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface/why-should-i-use-keyrings-instead-of-master-key-providers-and-master-keys.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/keyring-interface.md",
      "target_section": "why-should-i-use-keyrings-instead-of-master-key-providers-and-master-keys",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The local CMC MUST NOT store more entries than this value,\nexcept temporarily while performing a Put Cache Entry operation.\n",
      "id": "e9d3ada5e607625c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "The local CMC MUST NOT store more entries than this value, except temporarily while performing a Put Cache Entry operation.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/entry-capacity.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "entry-capacity",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The local CMC MUST accept entry capacity values between zero\nand an implementation-defined maximum, inclusive.\n",
      "id": "27fe9c102f5c4f3b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "The local CMC MUST accept entry capacity values between zero and an implementation-defined maximum, inclusive.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/entry-capacity.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "entry-capacity",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The _entry pruning tail size_\nis the number of least recently used entries that the local CMC\nMUST check during [pruning](#pruning)\nfor TTL-expired entries to evict.\n",
      "id": "142d0f5884641fe1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "The _entry pruning tail size_ is the number of least recently used entries that the local CMC MUST check during [pruning](#pruning) for TTL-expired entries to evict.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/entry-pruning-tail-size.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "entry-pruning-tail-size",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When performing a Get Cache Entry operation,\nthe local CMC MUST [prune TTL-expired cache entries](#pruning).\n",
      "id": "f3eb6f9a726e5d48",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "When performing a Get Cache Entry operation, the local CMC MUST [prune TTL-expired cache entries](#pruning).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/get-cache-entry.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "get-cache-entry",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The local CMC MUST NOT return any TTL-expired entry.\n",
      "id": "3f1e4a7db6943b4a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "The local CMC MUST NOT return any TTL-expired entry.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/get-cache-entry.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "get-cache-entry",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On initialization of the local CMC,\nthe caller MUST provide the following:\n",
      "id": "cfcca2d9f5ed6410",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "On initialization of the local CMC, the caller MUST provide the following:",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/initialization.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "initialization",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The local CMC MUST also define the following:\n",
      "id": "315d6e8e653bd20c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "The local CMC MUST also define the following:",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/initialization.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "initialization",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To prune TTL-expired cache entries,\nthe local CMC MUST evict all TTL-expired entries\namong the `N` least recently used entries,\nwhere `N` is the [Entry Pruning Tail Size](#entry-pruning-tail-size).\n",
      "id": "fc6a690cb1766d86",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "To prune TTL-expired cache entries, the local CMC MUST evict all TTL-expired entries among the `N` least recently used entries, where `N` is the [Entry Pruning Tail Size](#entry-pruning-tail-size).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/pruning.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "pruning",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The local CMC SHOULD also periodically evict all TTL-expired entries\namong the `N` least recently used entries.\n",
      "id": "9f82a0e288b84832",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "The local CMC SHOULD also periodically evict all TTL-expired entries among the `N` least recently used entries.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/pruning.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "pruning",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While performing a Put Cache Entry operation,\nthe local CMC MAY store more entries than the entry capacity.\n",
      "id": "9c453777441f6da6",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "While performing a Put Cache Entry operation, the local CMC MAY store more entries than the entry capacity.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/put-cache-entry.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "put-cache-entry",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, before returning, the local CMC MUST evict least-recently used entries\nuntil the number of stored entries does not exceed the entry capacity.\n",
      "id": "8e2d48a1ba8cf098",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "However, before returning, the local CMC MUST evict least-recently used entries until the number of stored entries does not exceed the entry capacity.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache/put-cache-entry.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md",
      "target_section": "put-cache-entry",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This specification defines the common behavior between the two implementations\nthat determine the REQUIRED functionality.\n",
      "id": "9caee6a4cafd9cd4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "This specification defines the common behavior between the two implementations that determine the REQUIRED functionality.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/consistency.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "consistency",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A master key SHOULD attempt to decrypt a data key using itself.\n",
      "id": "f2f2a72622b2fba7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "A master key SHOULD attempt to decrypt a data key using itself.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/decrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A master key MUST not attempt to use any other master keys.\n",
      "id": "2e5ce3c24838dbd5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "A master key MUST not attempt to use any other master keys.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/decrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The master key MUST encrypt the data key.\n",
      "id": "a8e31cedee11b562",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "The master key MUST encrypt the data key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/encrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "encrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Inputs to this interface MUST include\nthe algorithm suite,\nthe encryption context,\nthe encrypted data key,\nand information that can identify which master key\nwas used to encrypt the data key.\n",
      "id": "994c465b0956f699",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "Inputs to this interface MUST include the algorithm suite, the encryption context, the encrypted data key, and information that can identify which master key was used to encrypt the data key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/encrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "encrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The output of this interface MUST include\na value that this master key can use to obtain\nthe plaintext data key.\n",
      "id": "84a1e5291b971b63",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "The output of this interface MUST include a value that this master key can use to obtain the plaintext data key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/encrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "encrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the master key cannot encrypt the data key,\nthe call MUST result in an error.\n",
      "id": "282700c3b9e310de",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "If the master key cannot encrypt the data key, the call MUST result in an error.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/encrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "encrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The master key MUST generate a data key and MUST then encrypt that data key.\n",
      "id": "26d1fd2f14b039fb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "The master key MUST generate a data key and MUST then encrypt that data key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/generate-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "generate-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Inputs to this interface MUST include\nthe algorithm suite\nand the encryption context.\n",
      "id": "20591e8489b93fb5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "Inputs to this interface MUST include the algorithm suite and the encryption context.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/generate-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "generate-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The output of this interface MUST include\nthe plaintext data key,\nthe data key encrypted under the master key,\nand information that can identify which master key\nwas used to generate and encrypt the data key.\n",
      "id": "78aff514f89f46b4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "The output of this interface MUST include the plaintext data key, the data key encrypted under the master key, and information that can identify which master key was used to generate and encrypt the data key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/generate-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "generate-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the master key cannot generate or encrypt the data key,\nthe call MUST result in an error.\n",
      "id": "3b8d0cf759b685a1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "If the master key cannot generate or encrypt the data key, the call MUST result in an error.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/generate-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "generate-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A master key MUST supply itself and MUST NOT supply any other master keys.\n",
      "id": "4f5019be5276450d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "A master key MUST supply itself and MUST NOT supply any other master keys.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/get-master-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A master key MUST supply itself and MUST NOT supply any other master keys.\n",
      "id": "e7845aaeeba690f2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "A master key MUST supply itself and MUST NOT supply any other master keys.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/get-master-keys-for-encryption.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Master keys SHOULD NOT be included in any additional implementations.\n",
      "id": "980608e25d71b461",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "Master keys SHOULD NOT be included in any additional implementations.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/legacy.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "legacy",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any new implementations MUST include [Keyrings](./keyring-interface.md) instead.\n",
      "id": "9c5a9c8adf85a710",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Any new implementations MUST include [Keyrings](./keyring-interface.md) instead.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface/legacy.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-interface.md",
      "target_section": "legacy",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This specification defines the common behavior between the two implementations\nthat determine the REQUIRED functionality.\n",
      "id": "33ba061b5c512298",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "This specification defines the common behavior between the two implementations that determine the REQUIRED functionality.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/consistency.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "consistency",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The master key provider SHOULD attempt to decrypt the data key\nby passing the request to any master keys that it has access to\nuntil it has either exhausted available master keys\nor obtained a plaintext data key.\n",
      "id": "ecdb3f6e5e871bfa",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "The master key provider SHOULD attempt to decrypt the data key by passing the request to any master keys that it has access to until it has either exhausted available master keys or obtained a plaintext data key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/decrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Inputs to this interface MUST include\nthe algorithm suite,\nthe encryption context,\nand a list of encrypted data keys.\n",
      "id": "a9770cb61a79f744",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "Inputs to this interface MUST include the algorithm suite, the encryption context, and a list of encrypted data keys.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/decrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The output of this interface MUST include\nthe decrypted data key\nand information that can identify which master key\ndecrypted the data key.\n",
      "id": "8759eb6d527d8ee6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "The output of this interface MUST include the decrypted data key and information that can identify which master key decrypted the data key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/decrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the master key provider cannot decrypt the data key,\nthe call MUST result in an error.\n",
      "id": "c3ccfe7cd524c2b4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "If the master key provider cannot decrypt the data key, the call MUST result in an error.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/decrypt-data-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "decrypt-data-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An implementation MUST support master key selection by key ID.\n",
      "id": "597295b925c48521",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "An implementation MUST support master key selection by key ID.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An implementation MAY support master key selection by provider info or provider ID.\n",
      "id": "18c80a49ac8dbc36",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "An implementation MAY support master key selection by provider info or provider ID.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The output of this interface MUST be a master key.\n",
      "id": "eca3849356507d4c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "The output of this interface MUST be a master key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the master key provider cannot locate an appropriate master key,\nthe call MUST result in an error.\n",
      "id": "1ffad657ebcbab6d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "If the master key provider cannot locate an appropriate master key, the call MUST result in an error.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-key.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-key",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This interface provides a way for a master key provider to indicate which master keys\nSHOULD be used for encryption.\n",
      "id": "22ab62ce87d65810",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "This interface provides a way for a master key provider to indicate which master keys SHOULD be used for encryption.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-keys-for-encryption.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Inputs to this interface MUST include the encryption context.\n",
      "id": "0adc0c2967a193bc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "Inputs to this interface MUST include the encryption context.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-keys-for-encryption.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Inputs MAY include the plaintext body and plaintext size.\n",
      "id": "a70cd3003f0c8d51",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "Inputs MAY include the plaintext body and plaintext size.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-keys-for-encryption.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The output of this interface MUST include a list of all master keys that\nSHOULD be used for encryption.\n",
      "id": "c58d2f9dbf9dc253",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "The output of this interface MUST include a list of all master keys that SHOULD be used for encryption.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-keys-for-encryption.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The output of this interface MUST indicate which one of those master keys\nMUST be used to generate the data key.\n",
      "id": "34f9da175da63f05",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "The output of this interface MUST indicate which one of those master keys MUST be used to generate the data key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/get-master-keys-for-encryption.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Master key providers SHOULD NOT be included in any additional implementations.\n",
      "id": "6dc04ee51f461a3f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "Master key providers SHOULD NOT be included in any additional implementations.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/legacy.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "legacy",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any new implementations MUST include [Keyrings](./keyring-interface.md) instead.\n",
      "id": "d8a360e69fb219e4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Any new implementations MUST include [Keyrings](./keyring-interface.md) instead.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/legacy.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "legacy",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This MUST always be equal to the master key's key ID\nwith the exception of the raw AES master key.\n",
      "id": "518d509068127002",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "This MUST always be equal to the master key's key ID with the exception of the raw AES master key.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface/terms.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/master-key-provider-interface.md",
      "target_section": "terms",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this keyring does not have a [generator keyring](#generator-keyring), this list MUST NOT be empty.\n",
      "id": "ebafa8e219dbffcb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "If this keyring does not have a [generator keyring](#generator-keyring), this list MUST NOT be empty.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/child-keyrings.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "child-keyrings",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This keyring MUST implement the [Generate Data Key](keyring-interface.md#generate-data-key) behavior\nduring [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt).\n",
      "id": "be324af578c9f248",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "This keyring MUST implement the [Generate Data Key](keyring-interface.md#generate-data-key) behavior during [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/generator-keyring.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "generator-keyring",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This means that this keyring MUST return [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) containing\na plaintext data key on [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt).\n",
      "id": "c8e363e2d0a3e8d2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "This means that this keyring MUST return [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) containing a plaintext data key on [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/generator-keyring.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "generator-keyring",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the list of [child keyrings](#child-keyrings) is empty,\na [generator keyring](#generator-keyring) MUST be defined for the keyring.\n",
      "id": "37358b4b266c7d03",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "If the list of [child keyrings](#child-keyrings) is empty, a [generator keyring](#generator-keyring) MUST be defined for the keyring.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/generator-keyring.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "generator-keyring",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On keyring initialization, a keyring MUST define at least one of the following:\n",
      "id": "fe729497e193f57d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "On keyring initialization, a keyring MUST define at least one of the following:",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/inputs.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "inputs",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the decryption materials already contain a plaintext data key,\nthe keyring MUST fail\nand MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials).\n",
      "id": "36c316a26b9541f0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "If the decryption materials already contain a plaintext data key, the keyring MUST fail and MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Otherwise, OnDecrypt MUST first attempt to decrypt the [encrypted data keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-keys-1)\nin the input [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) using its\n[generator keyring](#generator-keyring).\n",
      "id": "324f4359084f52c7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Otherwise, OnDecrypt MUST first attempt to decrypt the [encrypted data keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-keys-1) in the input [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) using its [generator keyring](#generator-keyring).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the generator keyring is unable to decrypt\nthe materials, the multi-keyring MUST attempt to decrypt using its child keyrings,\nuntil one either succeeds in decryption or all have failed.\n",
      "id": "2778dc90fa839e16",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "If the generator keyring is unable to decrypt the materials, the multi-keyring MUST attempt to decrypt using its child keyrings, until one either succeeds in decryption or all have failed.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For each [keyring](keyring-interface.md) to be used for decryption,\nthe multi-keyring MUST call that keyring's [OnDecrypt](keyring-interface.md#ondecrypt) using\nthe unmodified [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) and the input\n[encrypted data key](structures.md#encrypted-data-key) list.\n",
      "id": "076a59623a1ee5b1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "For each [keyring](keyring-interface.md) to be used for decryption, the multi-keyring MUST call that keyring's [OnDecrypt](keyring-interface.md#ondecrypt) using the unmodified [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) and the input [encrypted data key](structures.md#encrypted-data-key) list.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If [OnDecrypt](keyring-interface.md#ondecrypt) returns [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials)\ncontaining a plaintext data key, the multi-keyring MUST immediately return the modified decryption materials.\n",
      "id": "35f7961f236a19c9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "If [OnDecrypt](keyring-interface.md#ondecrypt) returns [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) containing a plaintext data key, the multi-keyring MUST immediately return the modified decryption materials.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the child keyring's OnDecrypt call fails, the multi-keyring MUST collect the error and continue\nto the next keyring, if any.\n",
      "id": "9bf99e6973e884fc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "If the child keyring's OnDecrypt call fails, the multi-keyring MUST collect the error and continue to the next keyring, if any.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If, after calling [OnDecrypt](keyring-interface.md#ondecrypt) on every [child keyring](#child-keyrings)\n(and possibly the [generator keyring](#generator-keyring)), the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials)\nstill do not contain a plaintext data key, OnDecrypt MUST return a failure message containing the\ncollected failure messages from the child keyrings.\n",
      "id": "78e1abacf630dba4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "If, after calling [OnDecrypt](keyring-interface.md#ondecrypt) on every [child keyring](#child-keyrings) (and possibly the [generator keyring](#generator-keyring)), the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) still do not contain a plaintext data key, OnDecrypt MUST return a failure message containing the collected failure messages from the child keyrings.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this keyring has a generator keyring,\nthis keyring MUST first generate a plaintext data key using the generator keyring:\n",
      "id": "5bd813d4e989fdd0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "If this keyring has a generator keyring, this keyring MUST first generate a plaintext data key using the generator keyring:",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "- If the input encryption materials already include a plaintext data key,\nOnEncrypt MUST fail.\n",
      "id": "011b45acf88090fd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "- If the input encryption materials already include a plaintext data key, OnEncrypt MUST fail.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "- This keyring MUST first call the generator keyring's OnEncrypt\nusing the input encryption materials as input.\n",
      "id": "dd1b60287f4e7a3b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "- This keyring MUST first call the generator keyring's OnEncrypt using the input encryption materials as input.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "- If the generator keyring fails OnEncrypt,\nthis OnEncrypt MUST also fail.\n",
      "id": "f46bd85555e5fe65",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "- If the generator keyring fails OnEncrypt, this OnEncrypt MUST also fail.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "- If the generator keyring returns encryption materials missing a plaintext data key,\nOnEncrypt MUST fail.\n",
      "id": "0a934c0a1830053f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "- If the generator keyring returns encryption materials missing a plaintext data key, OnEncrypt MUST fail.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this keyring does not have a [generator keyring](#generator-keyring),\nand the input [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials)\ndoes not include a plaintext data key, OnEncrypt MUST fail.\n",
      "id": "3810fba5f03571fa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "If this keyring does not have a [generator keyring](#generator-keyring), and the input [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) does not include a plaintext data key, OnEncrypt MUST fail.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Next, for each [keyring](keyring-interface.md) in this keyring's list of [child keyrings](#child-keyrings),\nthe keyring MUST call [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt).\n",
      "id": "fefb096074c39705",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "Next, for each [keyring](keyring-interface.md) in this keyring's list of [child keyrings](#child-keyrings), the keyring MUST call [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the child keyring's [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt) fails, this OnEncrypt MUST also fail.\n",
      "id": "44d70cd41fb5b65b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "If the child keyring's [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt) fails, this OnEncrypt MUST also fail.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If all previous [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt) calls succeeded, this keyring MUST return\nthe [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) returned by the last OnEncrypt call.\n",
      "id": "3fc6a88a4ce84c21",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "If all previous [OnEncrypt](keyring-interface.md#onencrypt) calls succeeded, this keyring MUST return the [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) returned by the last OnEncrypt call.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/onencrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "onencrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Users SHOULD examine the [keyrings](keyring-interface.md) they include in a multi-keyring to ensure\nthat they understand what set of keyrings will be capable of obtaining the plaintext data key from\nthe returned set of encrypted data keys.\n",
      "id": "0f6e62aa5429e174",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "Users SHOULD examine the [keyrings](keyring-interface.md) they include in a multi-keyring to ensure that they understand what set of keyrings will be capable of obtaining the plaintext data key from the returned set of encrypted data keys.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring/security-considerations.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/multi-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "security-considerations",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This value MUST match the authentication tag length of the keyring's configured [wrapping algorithm](#wrapping-algorithm).\n",
      "id": "6a56ee98a204e626",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "This value MUST match the authentication tag length of the keyring's configured [wrapping algorithm](#wrapping-algorithm).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/authentication-tag-length.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "authentication-tag-length",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "- [Raw AES keyring MUST NOT accept a key namespace of \"aws-kms\".](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/issues/101)\n",
      "id": "d1be2c648396f34a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "- [Raw AES keyring MUST NOT accept a key namespace of \"aws-kms\".](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/issues/101)",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/changelog.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "changelog",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On keyring initialization,\nthe caller MUST provide the following:\n",
      "id": "3d1b5d3416caa771",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "On keyring initialization, the caller MUST provide the following:",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/initialization.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "initialization",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This value MUST match the IV length of the keyring's configured [wrapping algorithm](#wrapping-algorithm).\n",
      "id": "abe152dae9c5c6a0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "This value MUST match the IV length of the keyring's configured [wrapping algorithm](#wrapping-algorithm).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/iv-length.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "iv-length",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "OnDecrypt MUST take [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) and\na list of [encrypted data keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-key) as input.\n",
      "id": "6ede78007d594e87",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "OnDecrypt MUST take [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) and a list of [encrypted data keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-key) as input.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the decryption materials already contain a plaintext data key,\nthe keyring MUST fail\nand MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials).\n",
      "id": "caf3aae21b448df5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "If the decryption materials already contain a plaintext data key, the keyring MUST fail and MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The keyring MUST attempt to serialize the [decryption materials'](structures.md#decryption-materials)\n[encryption context](structures.md#encryption-context-1) according to the [encryption context serialization specification](structures.md#serialization).\n",
      "id": "84f205fc51f7dfdc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "The keyring MUST attempt to serialize the [decryption materials'](structures.md#decryption-materials) [encryption context](structures.md#encryption-context-1) according to the [encryption context serialization specification](structures.md#serialization).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the keyring cannot serialize the encryption context, OnDecrypt MUST fail.\n",
      "id": "66d3d902f59fa608",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "If the keyring cannot serialize the encryption context, OnDecrypt MUST fail.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The keyring MUST perform the following actions on each [encrypted data key](structures.md#encrypted-data-key)\nin the input encrypted data key list, serially, until it successfully decrypts one.\n",
      "id": "675d25cb919c849e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "The keyring MUST perform the following actions on each [encrypted data key](structures.md#encrypted-data-key) in the input encrypted data key list, serially, until it successfully decrypts one.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For each [encrypted data key](structures.md#encrypted-data-key),\nthe keyring MUST first attempt to deserialize the [serialized ciphertext](#ciphertext)\nto obtain the [encrypted key](#encrypted-key) and [authentication tag](#authentication-tag), and\ndeserialize the [serialized key provider info](#key-provider-information) to obtain the [key name](./keyring-interface.md#key-name),\n[IV](#iv), [IV length](#iv-length), and [authentication tag length](#authentication-tag-length).\n",
      "id": "74f2e178ca982346",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "For each [encrypted data key](structures.md#encrypted-data-key), the keyring MUST first attempt to deserialize the [serialized ciphertext](#ciphertext) to obtain the [encrypted key](#encrypted-key) and [authentication tag](#authentication-tag), and deserialize the [serialized key provider info](#key-provider-information) to obtain the [key name](./keyring-interface.md#key-name), [IV](#iv), [IV length](#iv-length), and [authentication tag length](#authentication-tag-length).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "- The [ciphertext](#ciphertext) and [key provider information](#key-provider-information) MUST be successfully deserialized.\n",
      "id": "823fe96b1e3a0f8b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "- The [ciphertext](#ciphertext) and [key provider information](#key-provider-information) MUST be successfully deserialized.",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "- The key name obtained from the encrypted data key's key provider information MUST have a value equal to this keyring's [key name](./keyring-interface.md#key-name).\n",
      "id": "f7bdea9431aa33dd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "- The key name obtained from the encrypted data key's key provider information MUST have a value equal to this keyring's [key name](./keyring-interface.md#key-name).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
      "target_path": "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring.md",
      "target_section": "ondecrypt",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "- The key provider ID of the encrypted data key MUST have a value equal to this keyring's [key namespace](./keyring-interface.md#key-namespace).\n",
      "id": "774087dacf53caf7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "- The key provider ID of the encrypted data key MUST have a value equal to this keyring's [key namespace](./keyring-interface.md#key-namespace).",
      "source": "compliance/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/raw-aes-keyring/ondecrypt.toml",
