  "specifications": {
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/algorithm-suites.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suites",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Algorithm Suites"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.4.0"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.4.0",
            "",
            "  - Reframe \"supported libraries\" as \"supported formats\"",
            "  - Add suites with symmetric signing",
            "  - Add DBE as supported format",
            "",
            "- 0.3.0",
            "  - [Material Providers Library (MPL)](../changes/2022-06-19_seperate_material_providers/change.md)"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language   | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation                                                                                                                                                      |",
            "| ---------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |",
            "| C          | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [cipher.c](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-c/blob/master/source/cipher.c)                                                                             |",
            "| NodeJS     | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [node_algorithms.ts](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-javascript/blob/master/modules/material-management/src/node_algorithms.ts)                       |",
            "| Browser JS | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [web_crypto_algorithms.ts](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-javascript/blob/master/modules/material-management/src/web_crypto_algorithms.ts)           |",
            "| Python     | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [identifiers.py](https://github.com/aws/aws-encryption-sdk-python/blob/master/src/aws_encryption_sdk/identifiers.py)                                                |",
            "| Java       | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [CryptoAlgorithm.java](https://github.com/aws/aws-encryption-sdk-java/blob/master/src/main/java/com/amazonaws/encryptionsdk/CryptoAlgorithm.java)                   |",
            "| Dafny      | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [AlgorithmSuites.dfy](https://github.com/aws/aws-encryption-sdk-dafny/blob/mainline/src/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/AlgorithmSuites.dfy)                      |",
            "| Java       | 0.3.0                                  | 0.3.0                     | [AlgorithmSuite.java](https://github.com/aws/amazon-s3-encryption-client-java/blob/main/src/main/java/software/amazon/encryption/s3/algorithms/AlgorithmSuite.java) |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "An algorithm suite is a collection of cryptographic algorithms and related values.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35d106897b5f27ce",
                  "9ef6d118a3ddcaec"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The algorithm suite defines the behaviors [supported formats](#supported-formats) MUST follow for cryptographic operations."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9ef6d118a3ddcaec"
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "aes",
          "lines": [
            "Specification: [NIST FIPS 297](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.197.pdf)",
            "",
            "The Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) is a symmetric block cipher encryption algorithm."
          ],
          "title": "AES"
        },
        {
          "id": "gcm",
          "lines": [
            "Specification: [NIST Special Publication 800-38D](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/SP/nistspecialpublication800-38d.pdf)",
            "",
            "Galois/Counter Mode is a mode of operation for block ciphers that provides authenticated encryption with additional data (AEAD).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d403f924a55bae43",
                  "17299bffddea9588"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If specified to use GCM, the AWS Encryption SDK MUST use GCM with the following specifics:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d403f924a55bae43"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- The internal block cipher is the encryption algorithm specified by the algorithm suite."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "17299bffddea9588"
          ],
          "title": "GCM"
        },
        {
          "id": "cbc",
          "lines": [
            "Specification: [NIST Special Publication 800-38A](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/legacy/sp/nistspecialpublication800-38a.pdf)",
            "",
            "Cipher Block Chaining is a mode of operation for symmetric key block ciphers that provides data confidentiality but does not provide authenticated encryption.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfb044ebbd91b862"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If specified to use CBC, the S3 Encryption Client MUST use CBC with the following specifics:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9dc3499602103fab"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- CBC MUST only be used to decrypt existing ciphertexts."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2e147ab491c67db1"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- CBC MUST NOT be used to encrypt new ciphertexts."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "cfb044ebbd91b862",
            "9dc3499602103fab",
            "2e147ab491c67db1"
          ],
          "title": "CBC"
        },
        {
          "id": "ctr",
          "lines": [
            "Specification: [NIST Special Publication 800-38A](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/legacy/sp/nistspecialpublication800-38a.pdf)",
            "",
            "Counter is a mode of operation for symmetric key block ciphers that provides data confidentiality but does not provide authenticated encryption.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8942ad8e1e261dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If specified to use CTR, the S3 Encryption Client MUST use CTR with the following specifics:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4688ad78160c2350"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- CTR MUST only be used to decrypt existing ciphertexts."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "24c9a51e4337480a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- CTR MUST NOT be used to encrypt new ciphertexts."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e8942ad8e1e261dd",
            "4688ad78160c2350",
            "24c9a51e4337480a"
          ],
          "title": "CTR"
        },
        {
          "id": "identity-kdf",
          "lines": [
            "The identity key derivation function (Identity KDF) is a key derivation algorithm.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e5e450e168d4e9e1"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The Identity KDF MUST take a byte sequence as input,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e5e450e168d4e9e1"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and MUST return the input, unchanged, as output."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ab83b0dcc1da496b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If included in the algorithm suite,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ab83b0dcc1da496b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the algorithm suite's encryption key length MUST equal the algorithm suite's [key derivation input length](#key-derivation-input-length)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e5e450e168d4e9e1",
            "e5e450e168d4e9e1",
            "ab83b0dcc1da496b",
            "ab83b0dcc1da496b"
          ],
          "title": "Identity KDF"
        },
        {
          "id": "hkdf",
          "lines": [
            "Specification: [RFC 5869](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5869)",
            "",
            "The HMAC-based extract-and-expand key derivation function (HKDF) is a key derivation algorithm."
          ],
          "title": "HKDF"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-formats",
          "lines": [
            "The following table inclues the cryptographic formats supported by the Material Providers Library.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1f72e8c1444aa241"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Both short and long name MUST be unique."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "| Cryptographic Format (long)                  | Cryptographic Format (short) |",
            "| -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |",
            "| AWS Encryption SDK Message Format            | ESDK                         |",
            "| S3 Encryption Client Cryptographic Format    | S3EC                         |",
            "| AWS Database Encryption Cryptographic Format | DBE                          |"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1f72e8c1444aa241"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Formats"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-format-algorithm-suites-enum",
          "lines": [
            "The following tables includes the algorithm suites",
            "supported by the Material Providers Library",
            "for each [supported format](#supported-formats).",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99b2d67c4abd5c7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The Material Providers Library MUST provide"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99b2d67c4abd5c7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "a set of algorithm suite ENUM for each [supported format](#supported-format)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "| ESDK Algorithm Suite ENUM                         |",
            "| ------------------------------------------------- |",
            "| ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                 |",
            "| ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                 |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                 |",
            "| ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256            |",
            "| ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256            |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256            |",
            "| ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256_ECDSA_P256 |",
            "| ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384 |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384 |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY            |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384 |",
            "",
            "| S3 EC Algorithm Suite ENUM        |",
            "| --------------------------------- |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_CBC_IV16_NO_KDF       |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_CTR_IV16_TAG16_NO_KDF |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF |",
            "",
            "| DBE Algorithm Suite ENUM                                             |",
            "| -------------------------------------------------------------------- |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384            |",
            "| ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384 |"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "99b2d67c4abd5c7c",
            "99b2d67c4abd5c7c"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Format Algorithm Suites ENUM"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-algorithm-suites-enum",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "261ed1d9ff6b97d7",
                  "576a147948ebd288"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The Material Providers Library MUST provide"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "261ed1d9ff6b97d7",
                  "576a147948ebd288"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "an ENUM that is the super set of all the [supported format algorithm suites enum](#supported-format-algorithm-suites-enum)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "261ed1d9ff6b97d7",
                  "576a147948ebd288"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "called the Algorithm Suite ENUM."
              }
            ],
            "In this specification this Algorithm Suite ENUM",
            "will be denoted as `Format.FormatENUM`",
            "to uniquely identify an Algorithm Suite ENUM across all supported formats.",
            "For example `ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF`",
            "is the Algorithm Suite ENUM for the ESDK Algorithm Suite ENUM `ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF`.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ae8c7dddcab4885",
                  "c46ea9d24ac8ee4f"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "This means that different formats MAY have duplicate Format Algorithm Suite ENUM."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "| Algorithm Suite ENUM                                                     |",
            "| ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384                   |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY                              |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                   |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                   |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256_ECDSA_P256                   |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                              |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                              |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                              |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CBC_IV16_NO_KDF                                         |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CTR_IV16_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   |",
            "| DBE.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384            |",
            "| DBE.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384 |"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "576a147948ebd288",
            "576a147948ebd288",
            "576a147948ebd288",
            "c46ea9d24ac8ee4f"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Algorithm Suites ENUM"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-algorithm-suites",
          "lines": [
            "The following table includes all supported algorithm suites.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ea0c31e31689ab0",
                  "66935db03ebc4e64"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The value `00 00` is reserved"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ea0c31e31689ab0",
                  "66935db03ebc4e64"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "and MUST NOT be used"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ea0c31e31689ab0",
                  "66935db03ebc4e64"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "as an Algorithm Suite ID in the future."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d37819659307991",
                  "39181c3d3d4e83fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Algorithm Suite ID MUST be a unique hex value across all supported algorithm suites."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "| Algorithm Suite ENUM                                                     | Algorithm Suite ID (hex) | Message Format Version | Algorithm Suite Data Length (bytes) |",
            "| ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------ | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------- |",
            "| DBE.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384            | 67 00                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| DBE.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384 | 67 01                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384                   | 05 78                    | 2.0                    | 32                                  |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY                              | 04 78                    | 2.0                    | 32                                  |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                   | 03 78                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                   | 03 46                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256_ECDSA_P256                   | 02 14                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                              | 01 78                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                              | 01 46                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                              | 01 14                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   | 00 78                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   | 00 46                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   | 00 14                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CBC_IV16_NO_KDF                                         | 00 70                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CTR_IV16_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   | 00 71                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                   | 00 72                    | 1.0                    | N/A                                 |"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "66935db03ebc4e64",
            "66935db03ebc4e64",
            "66935db03ebc4e64",
            "39181c3d3d4e83fc"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Algorithm Suites"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suites-encryption-key-derivation-settings",
          "lines": [
            "The following table includes key derivation information for supported algorithm suites.",
            "",
            "| Algorithm Suite ENUM                                                       | Key Derivation Input Length (bits) | Algorithm    | Hash Function | Salt Length (bits) | Key Commitment |",
            "| -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------ | ------------- | ------------------ | -------------- |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384            | 256                                | HKDF         | SHA-512       | N/A                | True           |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384 | 256                                | HKDF         | SHA-512       | N/A                | True           |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384                     | 256                                | HKDF         | SHA-512       | 256                | True           |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY                                | 256                                | HKDF         | SHA-512       | 256                | True           |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | 256                                | HKDF         | SHA-384       | 0                  | False          |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | 192                                | HKDF         | SHA-384       | 0                  | False          |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256_ECDSA_P256                     | 128                                | HKDF         | SHA-256       | 0                  | False          |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | 256                                | HKDF         | SHA-256       | 0                  | False          |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | 192                                | HKDF         | SHA-256       | 0                  | False          |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | 128                                | HKDF         | SHA-256       | 0                  | False          |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | 256                                | Identity KDF | N/A           | 0                  | False          |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | 192                                | Identity KDF | N/A           | 0                  | False          |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | 128                                | Identity KDF | N/A           | 0                  | False          |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CBC_IV16_NO_KDF                                           | 256                                | Identity KDF | N/A           | 0                  | False          |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CTR_IV16_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | 256                                | Identity KDF | N/A           | 0                  | False          |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | 256                                | Identity KDF | N/A           | 0                  | False          |"
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suites Encryption Key Derivation Settings"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suites-encryption-settings",
          "lines": [
            "The following table includes the encryption settings for supported algorithm suites.",
            "",
            "| Algorithm Suite ENUM                                                       | Encryption Algorithm | Encryption Algorithm Mode | Encryption Key Length (bits) | IV Length (bytes) | Authentication Tag Length (bytes) |",
            "| -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------- |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384            | AES                  | GCM                       | 256                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384 | AES                  | GCM                       | 256                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384                     | AES                  | GCM                       | 256                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY                                | AES                  | GCM                       | 256                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | AES                  | GCM                       | 256                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | AES                  | GCM                       | 192                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256_ECDSA_P256                     | AES                  | GCM                       | 128                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | AES                  | GCM                       | 256                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | AES                  | GCM                       | 192                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | AES                  | GCM                       | 128                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | AES                  | GCM                       | 256                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | AES                  | GCM                       | 192                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | AES                  | GCM                       | 128                          | 12                | 16                                |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CBC_IV16_NO_KDF                                           | AES                  | CBC                       | 256                          | 16                | N/A                               |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CTR_IV16_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | AES                  | CTR                       | 256                          | 16                | N/A                               |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | AES                  | GCM                       | 256                          | 12                | 16                                |"
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suites Encryption Settings"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suites-commit-key-derivation-settings",
          "lines": [
            "The following table includes commitment information for supported algorithm suites.",
            "These values are only relevant to algorithm suites that support [key commitment](#key-commitment).",
            "",
            "| Algorithm Suite ENUM                                                       | Key Derivation Input Length (bits) | Algorithm | Hash Function | Salt Length (bits) |",
            "| -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | --------- | ------------- | ------------------ |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384            | 256                                | HKDF      | SHA-512       | N/A                |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384 | 256                                | HKDF      | SHA-512       | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384                     | 256                                | HKDF      | SHA-512       | 256                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY                                | 256                                | HKDF      | SHA-512       | 256                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256_ECDSA_P256                     | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CBC_IV16_NO_KDF                                           | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CTR_IV16_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | N/A                                | N/A       | N/A           | N/A                |"
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suites Commit Key Derivation Settings"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suites-signature-settings",
          "lines": [
            "The following table includes signature information for supported algorithm suites.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4edc9c136dd523db",
                  "2f232a2e9971a559"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "An algorithm suite with a symmetric signature algorithm MUST use [intermediate key wrapping](#intermediate-key-wrapping)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "| Algorithm Suite ENUM                                                       | Asymmetric Signature Algorithm | Symmetric Signature Algorithm |",
            "| -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------- |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384            | Not applicable                 | HMAC with SHA-384             |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384 | ECDSA with P-384 and SHA-384   | HMAC with SHA-384             |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384                     | ECDSA with P-384 and SHA-384   | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY                                | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | ECDSA with P-384 and SHA-384   | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | ECDSA with P-384 and SHA-384   | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256_ECDSA_P256                     | ECDSA with P-256 and SHA-256   | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CBC_IV16_NO_KDF                                           | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CTR_IV16_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Not applicable                 | Not appliccable               |"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2f232a2e9971a559"
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suites Signature Settings"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suitees-edk-wrapping-settings",
          "lines": [
            "Based on the algorithm suite, there may be additional requirements to the wrapping and serialization of [encrypted data keys (EDKs)](./structures.md#encrypted-data-key).",
            "",
            "The following table includes EDK wrapping information for supported algorithm suites.",
            "",
            "| Algorithm Suite ENUM                                                       | EDK Wrapping Algorithm    |",
            "| -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384            | Intermediate Key Wrapping |",
            "| DDBEC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384_SYMSIG_HMAC_SHA384 | Intermediate Key Wrapping |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY_ECDSA_P384                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_HKDF_SHA512_COMMIT_KEY                                | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA384_ECDSA_P384                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256_ECDSA_P256                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_HKDF_SHA256                                | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_192_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| ESDK.ALG_AES_128_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CBC_IV16_NO_KDF                                           | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_CTR_IV16_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |",
            "| S3EC.ALG_AES_256_GCM_IV12_TAG16_NO_KDF                                     | Direct Key Wrapping       |"
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suitees EDK Wrapping Settings"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-edk-wrapping-algorithms",
          "lines": [
            "- [Direct Key Wrapping](#direct-key-wrapping)",
            "- [Intermediate Key Wrapping](#intermediate-key-wrapping)"
          ],
          "title": "Supported EDK Wrapping Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "id": "direct-key-wrapping",
          "lines": [
            "[Encrypted data keys](./structures.md#encrypted-data-key) produced under algorithms suites",
            "using Direct Key Wrapping have no additional requirements,",
            "other than those already perscribed by the [EDK Ciphertext specification](./structures.md#encrypted-data-key)."
          ],
          "title": "Direct Key Wrapping"
        },
        {
          "id": "intermediate-key-wrapping",
          "lines": [
            "For algorithm suites including symmetric signing, additional steps are needed in order to create material",
            "unique for each encrypted data key that can be used for symmetric signing.",
            "Through the creation of intermediate material during the key wrapping process,",
            "those with access to unwrap a particular encrypted data key also have access to symmetric signing material associated",
            "with that particular encrypted data key.",
            "With this property, a message can be created that is decryptable by several parties,",
            "but also signed by each party such that party A can be sure that the message was not",
            "updated by party B.",
            "Only those with the ability to wrap data keys for all parties are capable of",
            "creating messages that will be authenticated by all parties.",
            "",
            "[Encrypted data keys](./structures.md#encrypted-data-key) produced under algorithm suites using Intermediate Key Wrapping,",
            "have the following requirements:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "770f117423a3f32f",
                  "42f3768876867e24"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- For each encrypted data key, a distinct `intermediate key` MUST be generated using cryptographically secure random bytes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "42f7d02750cfb165"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This intermediate key MUST have length equal to the encryption key length of the algorithm suite."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4cba3234acd2f34c",
                  "fa1b8f5e041cb2da"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- For each encrypted data key, a [symmetric signing key](./structures.md#symmetric-signing-key) MUST be derived from the `intermediate key`"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4cba3234acd2f34c",
                  "fa1b8f5e041cb2da"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "using the key derivation algorithm in the algorithm suite, with the following specifics:"
              }
            ],
            "  - The input key material is the `intermediate key`",
            "  - The salt is empty",
            "  - The info is \"AWS_MPL_INTERMEDIATE_KEYWRAP_MAC\" as UTF8 bytes.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bee4a0bc453192cd",
                  "6c614d74338a7af9"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- For each encrypted data key, a `key encryption key` MUST be derived from the `intermediate key`"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bee4a0bc453192cd",
                  "6c614d74338a7af9"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "using the key derivation algorithm in the algorithm suite, with the following specifics:"
              }
            ],
            "  - The input key material is the `intermediate key`",
            "  - The salt is empty",
            "  - The info is \"AWS_MPL_INTERMEDIATE_KEYWRAP_ENC\" as UTF8 bytes.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc493ba5d163c238",
                  "3f0890599d86e57b"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The [EDK ciphertext](./structures.md#ciphertext) MUST be the following serialization:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "| Field                      | Length (bytes)                                     | Interpreted as |",
            "| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |",
            "| Wrapped Plaintext Data Key | The algorithm suite's encryption key length + 12   | Bytes          |",
            "| Wrapped Intermediate Key   | Determined by the keyring responsible for wrapping | Bytes          |"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "42f3768876867e24",
            "42f7d02750cfb165",
            "fa1b8f5e041cb2da",
            "fa1b8f5e041cb2da",
            "6c614d74338a7af9",
            "6c614d74338a7af9",
            "3f0890599d86e57b"
          ],
          "title": "Intermediate Key Wrapping"
        },
        {
          "id": "wrapped-plaintext-data-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "40e3b41a0d9c4966",
                  "da64546e19e9003b"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The wrapped plaintext data key MUST be the result of the following AES GCM 256 Encrypt operation:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- Plaintext: the [plaintext data key](./structures.md#plaintext-data-key) in the related encryption or decryption materials.",
            "- Encryption key: The `key encryption key` derived above.",
            "- AAD: The [encryption context](./structures.md#encryption-context) in the related encryption or decryption materials,",
            "  [serialized according to it's specification](structures.md#serialization).",
            "- IV: The IV is 0.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52cc4c8d7978b67a",
                  "18f5b1efd3209ed2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This value MUST be equal to the algorithm suite's encryption key length + 16."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "da64546e19e9003b",
            "18f5b1efd3209ed2"
          ],
          "title": "Wrapped Plaintext Data Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "wrapped-intermediate-key",
          "lines": [
            "The wrapped intermediate key has the same requirements for wrapping as the",
            "[EDK Ciphertext](./structures.md#encrypted-data-key) normally has under [Direct Key Wrapping](#direct-key-wrapping)."
          ],
          "title": "Wrapped Intermediate Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "structure",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4d9fa4d98a7615b6",
                  "a6e33c690b1b0d5b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The fields described below are REQUIRED to be specified by algorithm suites, unless otherwise specified."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "a6e33c690b1b0d5b"
          ],
          "title": "Structure"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suite-enum",
          "lines": [
            "A value that uniquely identifies an algorithm suite."
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suite ENUM"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suite-id",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6b9347bf69877d56",
                  "9cdbfe6870e27fc9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A 2-byte hex value that MUST uniquely identify an algorithm suite."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3471430c067508ec"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "This 2-byte value SHOULD be used to bind algorithm suites to ciphertext."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9cdbfe6870e27fc9",
            "3471430c067508ec"
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suite ID"
        },
        {
          "id": "encryption-algorithm",
          "lines": [
            "The block cipher encryption algorithm.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a00178fab97b53cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The length of the input encryption key MUST equal the [encryption key length](#encryption-key-length) specified by the algorithm suite."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "a00178fab97b53cf"
          ],
          "title": "Encryption Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-encryption-algorithms",
          "lines": [
            "- [AES](#aes)"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Encryption Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "id": "encryption-algorithm-mode",
          "lines": [
            "The AEAD operation mode used with the encryption algorithm.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3c7ef251009f679"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The length of the input IV MUST equal the IV length specified by the algorithm suite."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "934fbc236af5cff3"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The length of the authentication tag MUST equal the authentication tag length specified by the algorithm suite."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b3c7ef251009f679",
            "934fbc236af5cff3"
          ],
          "title": "Encryption Algorithm Mode"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-encryption-algorithm-modes",
          "lines": [
            "- [GCM](#gcm)",
            "- [CBC](#cbc) - legacy, decrypt-only",
            "- [CTR](#ctr) - legacy, decrypt-only"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Encryption Algorithm Modes"
        },
        {
          "id": "encryption-key-length",
          "lines": [
            "The length of the encryption key used as input to the encryption algorithm."
          ],
          "title": "Encryption Key Length"
        },
        {
          "id": "iv-length",
          "lines": [
            "The length of the initialization vector (IV) used with the encryption algorithm."
          ],
          "title": "IV Length"
        },
        {
          "id": "authentication-tag-length",
          "lines": [
            "The length of the authentication tag used with AEAD."
          ],
          "title": "Authentication Tag Length"
        },
        {
          "id": "encryption-key-derivation-algorithm",
          "lines": [
            "This key derivation algorithm defines what key derivation function (KDF) to use for encryption key generation.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e82f553afb927e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The specified KDF algorithm MUST be used to generate the encryption algorithm encryption key input."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6e82f553afb927e6"
          ],
          "title": "Encryption Key Derivation Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-encryption-key-derivation-algorithms",
          "lines": [
            "- [Identity KDF](#identity-kdf)",
            "- [HKDF](./transitive-requirements.md#hkdf-encryption-key)"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Encryption Key Derivation Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "id": "key-derivation-input-length",
          "lines": [
            "The length of the input to the Key Derivation Algorithm."
          ],
          "title": "Key Derivation Input Length"
        },
        {
          "id": "key-commitment",
          "lines": [
            "AES-GCM is not key committing by default.",
            "Key commitment is a property,",
            "which ensures that exactly one data key can be used to decrypt a ciphertext.",
            "However, not all algorithm suites provide this property."
          ],
          "title": "Key Commitment"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-key-commitment-values",
          "lines": [
            "- True",
            "- False"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Key Commitment Values"
        },
        {
          "id": "commit-key",
          "lines": [
            "A key that is used to provide [key commitment](#key-commitment) to AES-GCM."
          ],
          "title": "Commit Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "commit-key-derivation-algorithm",
          "lines": [
            "This key derivation algorithm defines what key derivation function (KDF) to use for commitment key generation.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b966c09618025fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The specified KDF algorithm MUST be used to generate the [commit key](#commit-key)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "0b966c09618025fe"
          ],
          "title": "Commit Key Derivation Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-commit-key-derivation-algorithm",
          "lines": [
            "- [HKDF](./transitive-requirements.md#hkdf-commit-key)"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Commit Key Derivation Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "commit-key-length",
          "lines": [
            "The length of the commit key used to verify [key commitment](#key-commitment)."
          ],
          "title": "Commit Key Length"
        },
        {
          "id": "asymmetric-signature-algorithm",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c61c02e79873be6",
                  "b7535a7bf19b2f00"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "This field is OPTIONAL."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "The asymmetric signature algorithm defines what asymmetric algorithm to use for asymmetric signature generation and verification.",
            "",
            "If the algorithm suite includes an asymmetric signature algorithm:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6c18e7e653722d85"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Asymmetric signatures MUST be generated using the specified asymmetric signature algorithm."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ed6fd882f954fbce"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Asymmetric signatures MUST be verified using the specified asymmetric signature algorithm."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "If the algorithm suite does not include a asymmetric signature algorithm:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ab6cb5a21c4c36c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Asymmetric signatures MUST NOT be generated."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "59b46a8b5c080021"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Asymmetric signatures MUST NOT be verified."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b7535a7bf19b2f00",
            "6c18e7e653722d85",
            "ed6fd882f954fbce",
            "8ab6cb5a21c4c36c",
            "59b46a8b5c080021"
          ],
          "title": "Asymmetric Signature Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-asymmetric-signature-algorithms",
          "lines": [
            "- [ECDSA with P256 and SHA256](./transitive-requirements.md#ecdsa)",
            "- [ECDSA with P384 and SHA384](./transitive-requirements.md#ecdsa)"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Asymmetric Signature Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "id": "symmetric-signature-algorithm",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0d4afccc74a82b5a",
                  "6bdcb9516f2d4225"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "This field is OPTIONAL."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "The symmetric signature algorithm defines what symmetric algorithm to use for symmetric signature generation and verification.",
            "",
            "If the algorithm suite includes an symmetric signature algorithm:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "380db08ee0951c77"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Symmetric signatures MUST be generated using the specified symmetric signature algorithm."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e9795d840b05098"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Symmetric signatures MUST be verified using the specified symmetric signature algorithm."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "77bb46a7436d7a8a",
                  "5e6c91db6682abbe"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The algorithm suite MUST also use [Intermediate Key Wrapping](#intermediate-key-wrapping)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "If the algorithm suite does not include a symmetric signature algorithm:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "586e1f9fc3f7ad43"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Symmetric signatures MUST NOT be generated."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "310bccfa083eed80"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Symmetric signatures MUST NOT be verified."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6bdcb9516f2d4225",
            "380db08ee0951c77",
            "7e9795d840b05098",
            "5e6c91db6682abbe",
            "586e1f9fc3f7ad43",
            "310bccfa083eed80"
          ],
          "title": "Symmetric Signature Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-symmetric-signature-algorithms",
          "lines": [
            "- [HMAC](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2104) with [SHA384](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6234)"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Symmetric Signature Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "id": "message-format-version",
          "lines": [
            "Indicates the serialization or message format version for the supported algorithm suite.",
            "This value can be duplicated across [supported formats](#supported-formats).",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9afebf373e4490c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This MUST be used to branch any serialization/deserialization logic in [supported formats](#supported-formats)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9afebf373e4490c6"
          ],
          "title": "Message Format Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-message-format-version",
          "lines": [
            "**ESDK**",
            "",
            "- 1.0",
            "- 2.0",
            "",
            "**S3EC**",
            "",
            "- 1.0",
            "",
            "**DDBEC**",
            "",
            "- 1.0"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Message Format Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suite-data",
          "lines": [
            "Algorithm suites may capture a variable-per-algorithm-suite length of data",
            "relevant to that algorithm suite’s mode of operation."
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suite Data"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-algorithm-suite-data",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23d45f4ac25893bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Algorithm Suite 05 78 MUST store the commit key in the suite data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a48266dfd73e010"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Algorithm Suite 04 78 MUST store the commit key in the suite data"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "23d45f4ac25893bd",
            "9a48266dfd73e010"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Algorithm Suite Data"
        },
        {
          "id": "algorithm-suite-data-length",
          "lines": [
            "Then length of the [algorithm suite data](#algorithm-suite-data).",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f0e11f8201f843f"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The field MAY be length 0."
              }
            ],
            "Its length and how the contents are used",
            "are determined by the algorithm suite.",
            "Where the contents are stored is determined by the message format."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8f0e11f8201f843f"
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Suite Data Length"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-algorithm-suite-data-lengths",
          "lines": [
            "- 32"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Algorithm Suite Data Lengths"
        },
        {
          "id": "security-considerations",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Security Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "which-algorithm-suite-should-i-use",
          "lines": [
            "You should use the default algorithm suite.",
            "",
            "You should use an algorithm suite that supports key commitment.",
            "",
            "You may use the non-default AES-GCM with key derivation and signing key algorithm suites",
            "if key derivation input lengths of other sizes are required.",
            "",
            "If the users who encrypt and the users who decrypt are equally trusted,",
            "you may use AES-GCM with only key derivation algorithm suites.",
            "",
            "You should not use AES-GCM with only key derivation algorithm suites",
            "if the users who encrypt and the users who decrypt are not equally trusted.",
            "",
            "You should not use AES-GCM without key Derivation or signing,",
            "except for backwards compatibility.",
            "",
            "You should not use AES-CBC unless you need to decrypt legacy ciphertexts encrypted using AES-CBC.",
            "",
            "You should not use AES-CTR unless you need to perform partial decryption of a ciphertext object encrypted using AES-GCM in a client that does not support a safe mode of partial ciphertext decryption."
          ],
          "title": "Which algorithm suite should I use?"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Algorithm Suites"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-discovery-keyring.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-discovery-keyring",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS Discovery Keyring"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.3.0"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.3.0",
            "",
            "  - Incorporate [KMS Keyring Redesign](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/tree/master/proposals/2020-07-01_aws-kms-keyring-redesign)",
            "",
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Rename Key IDs to Key Names for increased clarity",
            "  - Update Key Names and Generator sections to reinforce support for all AWS KMS key identifiers",
            "  - [Pull request link for discussions](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/pull/123)",
            "",
            "- 0.2.1",
            "",
            "  - [Clarify naming of KMS to AWS KMS](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/issues/67)",
            "",
            "- 0.2.0",
            "",
            "  - [Remove Keyring Trace](../changes/2020-05-13_remove-keyring-trace/change.md)",
            "",
            "- 0.1.0-preview",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "A keyring which interacts with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)",
            "to decrypt data keys using a filter to identify Customer Master Keys (CMKs)."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "interface",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79dd1619cf354a00",
                  "957a53ca2d7a90c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST implement that [AWS Encryption SDK Keyring interface](../keyring-interface.md#interface)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "957a53ca2d7a90c9"
          ],
          "title": "Interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0aef2f65df85920c",
                  "7e947565885cc4c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "On initialization the caller MUST provide:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- An AWS KMS client",
            "- An optional discovery filter that is an AWS partition and a set of AWS accounts",
            "- An optional list of AWS KMS grant tokens",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "069b91f8ae4394d0",
                  "87d4715e22889b6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The AWS KMS SDK client MUST NOT be null."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7e947565885cc4c9",
            "87d4715e22889b6b"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "onencrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22fc6606c463979d",
                  "7f3cfcf22ea447fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This function MUST fail."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7f3cfcf22ea447fa"
          ],
          "title": "OnEncrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "ondecrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "327aac17e9a1584e",
                  "8e9ce2626f40ea73"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST take [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "327aac17e9a1584e",
                  "8e9ce2626f40ea73"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "a list of [encrypted data keys](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10819816a901536f",
                  "99efd1e9f05e6d15"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) already contained a valid plaintext data key,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10819816a901536f",
                  "99efd1e9f05e6d15"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "they keyring MUST fail and MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9ed83d6fb278c83",
                  "900c3c2026712923",
                  "705eb5df5ba23bbf"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The set of encrypted data keys MUST first be filtered to match this keyring’s configuration."
              }
            ],
            "For the encrypted data key to match",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0c71b7f3d6238fc3",
                  "ef47ba5ef274087d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- Its provider ID MUST exactly match the value “aws-kms”."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33c42e312c5c8a7e",
                  "9ae5a6cd7a76e030"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "- The provider info MUST be a [valid AWS KMS ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn) with a resource type of `key` or OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7349185b6749b32d",
                  "3b87b498bdd997ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- If a discovery filter is configured, its partition and the provider info partition MUST match."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88e70634588ce8a9",
                  "d0483ffb7c01c171"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- If a discovery filter is configured, its set of accounts MUST contain the provider info account."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7696ee3b16e7de03",
                  "e678fd32fe5f2758"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "For each encrypted data key in the filtered set, one at a time, the OnDecrypt MUST attempt to decrypt the data key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " If this attempt results in an error, then these errors are collected."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c97887462d1bb38",
                  "5b2cc308cc17358e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "To attempt to decrypt a particular [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c97887462d1bb38",
                  "5b2cc308cc17358e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST call [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) with the configured AWS KMS client."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9c6637a87a338b26",
                  "42a5e7cf61b3dd03"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "When calling [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html), the keyring MUST call with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- `KeyId`: The AWS KMS ARN from the provider info",
            "- `CiphertextBlob`: The [encrypted data key ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext).",
            "- `EncryptionContext`: The [encryption context](../structures.md#encryption-context) included in the input [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials).",
            "- `GrantTokens`: this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)",
            "",
            "If the call to [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) succeeds OnDecrypt verifies",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "27692b398d15aca0",
                  "9d20ff6fe2e6623a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- The `KeyId` field in the response MUST equal the AWS KMS ARN from the provider info"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe87c5a1e06d8a7c",
                  "3e0a533c528b3cd0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- The length of the response’s `Plaintext` MUST equal the [key derivation input length](../algorithm-suites.md#key-derivation-input-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe87c5a1e06d8a7c",
                  "3e0a533c528b3cd0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "specified by the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md) included in the input [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c83548b94aceb173",
                  "1babe1da17e8ca02"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the response does not satisfy these requirements"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c83548b94aceb173",
                  "1babe1da17e8ca02"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "then an error is collected and the next encrypted data key in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30330573cfb34a52",
                  "bcbf155529d785e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the response does satisfy these requirements then OnDecrypt MUST do the following with the response:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- set the plaintext data key on the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) as the response `Plaintext`.",
            "- immediately return the modified [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f4455aa8e13cf2e",
                  "90e06db037d787f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If OnDecrypt fails to successfully decrypt any [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f4455aa8e13cf2e",
                  "90e06db037d787f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "then it MUST yield an error that includes all collected errors."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8e9ce2626f40ea73",
            "8e9ce2626f40ea73",
            "99efd1e9f05e6d15",
            "99efd1e9f05e6d15",
            "705eb5df5ba23bbf",
            "ef47ba5ef274087d",
            "9ae5a6cd7a76e030",
            "3b87b498bdd997ef",
            "d0483ffb7c01c171",
            "e678fd32fe5f2758",
            "5b2cc308cc17358e",
            "5b2cc308cc17358e",
            "42a5e7cf61b3dd03",
            "9d20ff6fe2e6623a",
            "3e0a533c528b3cd0",
            "3e0a533c528b3cd0",
            "1babe1da17e8ca02",
            "1babe1da17e8ca02",
            "bcbf155529d785e8",
            "90e06db037d787f2",
            "90e06db037d787f2"
          ],
          "title": "OnDecrypt"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS Discovery Keyring"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-ecdh-keyring.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-ecdh-keyring",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS ECDH Keyring"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.1.0-preview"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.1.0-preview",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "A keyring which does local ECDH to",
            "establish a shared secret that can be used to derive shared wrapping keys for",
            "encryption and decryption of data keys."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "ecdh",
          "lines": [
            "ECDH (Elliptic-curve Diffie–Hellman) is a key agreement protocol that",
            "allows two parties, each having an elliptic-curve public–private key",
            "pair, to establish a shared secret over an insecure channel.",
            "",
            "This shared secret may be directly used as a key, or to derive another key."
          ],
          "title": "ECDH"
        },
        {
          "id": "ecc-keys",
          "lines": [
            "ECC (Elliptic Curve Cryptography) are keys that are generated from elliptic",
            "curves over finite fields.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b92e158ae7b9c65b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "ECC Private Key MUST be a [PEM encoded PKCS #8 PrivateKeyInfo structures](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5958#section-2)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b92e158ae7b9c65b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "as private key."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c1861e4752f36251"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "ECC Public Key MUST be a [DER-encoded ASN.1 SubjectPublicKeyInfo](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5280#section-4.1)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b92e158ae7b9c65b",
            "b92e158ae7b9c65b",
            "c1861e4752f36251"
          ],
          "title": "ECC Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "interface",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cef5dc43b7e8bdc6",
                  "8789fbc839feeaeb"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST implement the [AWS Encryption SDK Keyring interface](../keyring-interface.md#interface)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8789fbc839feeaeb"
          ],
          "title": "Interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            "On keyring initialization,",
            "the caller:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "710e9fcf9a790167",
                  "347b05368d175dc1"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST provide a [Key Agreement Schema](#key-agreement-schema)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f4c1b76206611614",
                  "4a62b9d9a6c4705c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST provide a [Curve Specification](#curve-specification)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fd54805e7d54d9f0",
                  "b563d56521a12093"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST provide an AWS KMS SDK client"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "On keyring initialization,",
            "the caller:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "541d11c6da174e6c",
                  "45b8e0a1e3f52d05"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "- MAY provide a list of Grant Tokens"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ed9afd64b61cb87b",
                  "f46fe9ef5adf5580"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the keyring MUST set the recipient's public key on the keyring."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "347b05368d175dc1",
            "4a62b9d9a6c4705c",
            "b563d56521a12093",
            "45b8e0a1e3f52d05",
            "f46fe9ef5adf5580"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "curve-specification",
          "lines": [
            "The ECDH curve specification to use with this keyring.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ec4b5cb7f21037d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This value MUST correspond with one of the [supported curve specifications](#supported-curve-specifications)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6ec4b5cb7f21037d"
          ],
          "title": "Curve Specification"
        },
        {
          "id": "supported-curve-specifications",
          "lines": [
            "The following curve specifications are currently defined:",
            "",
            "- [ECC NIST P256](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.186-5.pdf#page=29)",
            "- [ECC NIST P384](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.186-5.pdf#page=29)",
            "- [ECC NIST P521](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.186-5.pdf#page=29)",
            "- [SM2](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/asymmetric-key-specs.html#key-spec-sm)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e3efae1e7abb16b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This keyring MUST NOT use a curve specification outside of the defined above."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1e3efae1e7abb16b"
          ],
          "title": "Supported Curve Specifications"
        },
        {
          "id": "key-agreement-schema",
          "lines": [
            "The following Key Agreement Schemas are currently supported for an AWS ECDH Keyring:",
            "",
            "- [KmsPublicKeyDiscovery](../key-agreement-schemas.md#kmspublickeydiscovery)",
            "- [KmsPrivateKeyToStaticPublicKey](../key-agreement-schemas.md#kmsprivatekeytostaticpublickey)"
          ],
          "title": "Key Agreement Schema"
        },
        {
          "id": "key-agreement-procedure",
          "lines": [
            "Depending on the configured [Key Agreement](./key-agreement-schemas.md#supported-key-agreement-schemas)",
            "Schema, the shared secret is computed differently."
          ],
          "title": "Key Agreement Procedure"
        },
        {
          "id": "key-derivation-function-configuration",
          "lines": [
            "An AWS ECDH Key Derivation Function Configuration is defined as:",
            "",
            "- Key Derivation Function:",
            "  - [Counter-Mode](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-108r1-upd1.pdf#page=14)",
            "- Key Derivation Method:",
            "  - HMAC_SHA384"
          ],
          "title": "Key Derivation Function Configuration"
        },
        {
          "id": "additional-information",
          "lines": [
            "The keyring will use the encryption and decryption materials' encryption",
            "context in two places.",
            "",
            "1. Fixed Info as part of the KDF",
            "   - This ensures that the shared wrapping key is cryptographically",
            "     bound in context to what it will be used for.",
            "1. AAD as part of the data key wrapping",
            "   - As with the other keyrings, the ECDH keyring will use",
            "     the supplied encryption context to also cryptographically bind",
            "     the shared wrapping key to the data key.",
            "",
            "Both the KDF and the AES-GCM operations will construct",
            "a serialized AdditionalInfoAAD that will be include",
            "the FixedInfo and the AAD.",
            "This allows the AAD and the FixedInfo",
            "to be bound to the shared wrapping key AND the",
            "AAD in the AES-GCM data key wrapping operation.",
            "",
            "Using additional information in this way allows",
            "customers to have authenticated encryption",
            "because the additional information",
            "must match in the derivation step",
            "and the data key wrapping/unwrapping step in order to",
            "produce the data encryption key.",
            "",
            "The additional information is a key-value mapping of arbitrary, non-secret, UTF-8 encoded strings.",
            "",
            "[Encryption Context](../structures.md#encryption-context) is used as additional information",
            "as part of the fixed info field input to the KDF. As such, users",
            "should use the Additional Information to store:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec235c5be770cd5c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Non-secret data that MUST remain associated with the [message](../data-format/message.md) ciphertext."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "ec235c5be770cd5c"
          ],
          "title": "Additional Information"
        },
        {
          "id": "structure",
          "lines": [
            "Since messages encrypted the AWS KMS ECDH Keyring can be decrypted by the",
            "RAW ECDH Keyring both the Key Provider Information and the Ciphertext structures",
            "are serialized the same in both keyrings. See each section in the RAW ECDH Keyring",
            "[specification](../raw-ecdh-keyring.md#structure)."
          ],
          "title": "Structure"
        },
        {
          "id": "key-provider-information-raw-ecdh-keyring-md-key-provider-information",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Key Provider Information](../raw-ecdh-keyring.md#key-provider-information)"
        },
        {
          "id": "ciphertext-raw-ecdh-keyring-md-ciphertext",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Ciphertext](../raw-ecdh-keyring.md#ciphertext)"
        },
        {
          "id": "operation",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Operation"
        },
        {
          "id": "onencrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3508db7da853b97c",
                  "4005a95f2053ac6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST fail if configured with a [KmsPublicKeyDiscovery Key Agreement Configuration](../key-agreement-schemas.md#kmspublickeydiscovery)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6c87d1c7e67b44ca",
                  "1b20f120f9fefc3c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST take [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e45f27cc479b21d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The keyring MUST attempt to serialize the [encryption materials'](structures.md#encryption-materials)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e45f27cc479b21d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "[encryption context](structures.md#encryption-context-1) according to the [encryption context serialization specification](structures.md#serialization)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "49a6663a6a015401",
                  "765de31501a09bfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the keyring cannot serialize the encryption context, OnEncrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "940587204c766155",
                  "29080f866e53a34d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "To attempt to generate a shared secret,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "940587204c766155",
                  "29080f866e53a34d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST call [AWS KMS DeriveSharedSecret]()"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "940587204c766155",
                  "29080f866e53a34d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the keyring MUST call with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c731510e1bd5944",
                  "b4b96ca3ae7f5b1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `KeyId` MUST be the configured AWS KMS key identifier in the schema"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e2c170d361a7dd1",
                  "6366ebf188235a04"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `PublicKey` MUST be the configured Recipient Public Key on the schema"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "725f8fdf4e94f305",
                  "c0445a89e9746353"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `KeyAgreementAlgorithm` MUST be \"ECDH\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "634c33598d990463",
                  "0de4d5bf28070e95"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `GrantTokens` MUST be this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "68e831f702fda65a",
                  "1d1528bc68f88557",
                  "94c529508a79db63"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "If the call to KMS DeriveSharedSecret fails, the keyring MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e65ce1930c16c02",
                  "07e2f44e9afbc130"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The keyring MUST derive a shared wrapping key according to the construction"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e65ce1930c16c02",
                  "07e2f44e9afbc130"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "outlined by the [key agreement schemas](./key-agreement-schemas.md#key-derivation)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9af910613dfdea66"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the Key Derivation step fails, OnEncrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "382ec8a617f3ffae",
                  "f9852c5804c19ec0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If they Key Derivation step succeeds it MUST produce"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "382ec8a617f3ffae",
                  "f9852c5804c19ec0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "keying material with a length of 64 bytes."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d019500ec53f22c",
                  "7438074e8bddc7b6"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The keyring MUST use the first 32 bytes as the Commitment Key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eec3eab6ddb1f5d7",
                  "9c6e0850f42ef88c"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The keyring MUST use the last 32 bytes as the Shared Wrapping Key."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6e713184c493404",
                  "5ff669e4bbb4ee4d"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The keyring MUST perform data key wrapping according to the [Data Key Wrapping section](../raw-ecdh-keyring.md#data-key-wrapping)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d8afdbdff7204ae6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the keyring is unable to wrap a plaintext data key, OnEncrypt MUST fail"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d8afdbdff7204ae6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and MUST NOT modify the [encryption materials](structures.md#encryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2f18164b4a5e3de7"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Otherwise, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aaf1d18656bed154",
                  "da8467c0940a2aa8",
                  "2f18164b4a5e3de7"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST append a new [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aaf1d18656bed154",
                  "da8467c0940a2aa8",
                  "2f18164b4a5e3de7"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "to the encrypted data key list in the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2f18164b4a5e3de7"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": ", constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "96ad8d1eb2463ebd",
                  "f5886269d46d4ba7"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The [key provider id](../structures.md#key-provider-id) MUST be the UTF8 encoded string \"aws-kms-ecdh\"."
              }
            ],
            "- The [key provider information](structures.md#key-provider-information) is serialized as the",
            "  [raw ECDH keyring key provider information](../raw-ecdh-keyring.md#key-provider-information).",
            "- The [ciphertext](structures.md#ciphertext) is serialized as the",
            "  [raw ECDH keyring ciphertext](../raw-ecdh-keyring.md#ciphertext)."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4005a95f2053ac6a",
            "1b20f120f9fefc3c",
            "5e45f27cc479b21d",
            "5e45f27cc479b21d",
            "765de31501a09bfe",
            "29080f866e53a34d",
            "29080f866e53a34d",
            "29080f866e53a34d",
            "b4b96ca3ae7f5b1e",
            "6366ebf188235a04",
            "c0445a89e9746353",
            "0de4d5bf28070e95",
            "94c529508a79db63",
            "07e2f44e9afbc130",
            "07e2f44e9afbc130",
            "9af910613dfdea66",
            "f9852c5804c19ec0",
            "f9852c5804c19ec0",
            "7438074e8bddc7b6",
            "9c6e0850f42ef88c",
            "5ff669e4bbb4ee4d",
            "d8afdbdff7204ae6",
            "d8afdbdff7204ae6",
            "2f18164b4a5e3de7",
            "2f18164b4a5e3de7",
            "f5886269d46d4ba7"
          ],
          "title": "OnEncrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "ondecrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "40933d529f002345"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST take [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials) and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "40933d529f002345"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "a list of [encrypted data keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-key) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ba016afafec0abb",
                  "6c5f3c994525172b"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the decryption materials already contain a plaintext data key,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ba016afafec0abb",
                  "6c5f3c994525172b"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST fail"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ba016afafec0abb",
                  "6c5f3c994525172b"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "and MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c83da62f3d6f08bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The keyring MUST attempt to serialize the [decryption materials'](structures.md#decryption-materials)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c83da62f3d6f08bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "[encryption context](structures.md#encryption-context-1) according to the [encryption context serialization specification](structures.md#serialization)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc47b71496198213"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the keyring cannot serialize the encryption context, OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72c6f74ddbda19a7",
                  "5c9cc251586d8e85"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The set of encrypted data keys MUST first be filtered to match this keyring’s configuration."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72c6f74ddbda19a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "For the encrypted data key to match:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61469b891b3cd1dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- MUST first verify that the uncompressed deserialized sender's public key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61469b891b3cd1dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and the uncompressed deserialized recipient's public key match the public"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61469b891b3cd1dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "keys configured on the keyring."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a0ad97ec2df7165"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The deserialized version value in the [key provider information](#key-provider-information) MUST match `0x01`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8da40ba84864ac2",
                  "c84b8d1e2803b373"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The [ciphertext](#ciphertext) and [key provider information](#key-provider-information) MUST be successfully deserialized."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a38eb114b71a8fc",
                  "acc53df814b2f6ba"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The key provider ID of the encrypted data key MUST have a value equal to the UTF8 encoded strings `raw-ecdh` OR `aws-kms-ecdh`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b6c33a3c85bf810"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The [authentication tag length](#authentication-tag-length) obtained from the key provider information MUST have a value equal to 16 bytes."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d16f8262bdc1ddfd",
                  "c2e1b0a668365823"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "For each encrypted data key in the filtered set, one at a time, the OnDecrypt MUST attempt to decrypt the data key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d16f8262bdc1ddfd",
                  "50be267dcbe5d282"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If this attempt results in an error, then these errors MUST be collected."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c34efc99ddc3114"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "To attempt to decrypt a particular [encrypted data key](./structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c34efc99ddc3114"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST attempt to deserialize the [serialized ciphertext](#ciphertext)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c34efc99ddc3114"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "to obtain:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- The derivation nonce",
            "- The commitment key",
            "- The [encrypted key](#encrypted-key)",
            "- The [authentication tag](#authentication-tag)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7fded9bc99bd1e5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the keyring is unable to deserialize this information then an error MUST be collected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7fded9bc99bd1e5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and the next encrypted data key in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7f215ff3a2837cd",
                  "fc540e0009bd10e5"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The keyring MUST derive the shared secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7f215ff3a2837cd",
                  "fc540e0009bd10e5"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "by calling [AWS KMS DeriveSharedSecret]()"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fc540e0009bd10e5"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bbf0b2ee6d77038d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- `KeyId` MUST be the configured AWS KMS key identifier in the schema"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ed7e6781d9170726"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- `PublicKey` MUST be the configured Recipient Public Key on the schema"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4811e577274de98e"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- `KeyAgreementAlgorithm` MUST be \"ECDH\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "181c419b082c7a68"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- `GrantTokens` MUST be this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0bc0ba6f326ff103"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the call to KMS DeriveSharedSecret fails, an error MUST be collected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0bc0ba6f326ff103"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and the next encrypted data key in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc6f91e8e29029f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The keyring MUST derive a shared wrapping key according"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cc6f91e8e29029f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "to the construction outlined by the [key agreement schemas](./key-agreement-schemas.md#key-derivation)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2dd45a078b58f8d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the Key Derivation step fails, then an error MUST be collected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2dd45a078b58f8d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and the next encrypted data key in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0e96b9ff3aaebd86"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If they Key Derivation step succeeds it MUST produce"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0e96b9ff3aaebd86"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "keying material with a length of 64 bytes."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e93099f56096e2ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The keyring MUST use the first 32 bytes as the Commitment Key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c44be1b73a4232bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The keyring MUST use the last 32 bytes as the Shared Wrapping Key."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43ed96077249cb2f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The keyring MUST check that the calculated Commitment Key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43ed96077249cb2f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "from the key derivation step is equal to the deserialized commitment key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43ed96077249cb2f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "found in the encrypted data key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2069003d6011471c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This check MUST be a constant time check."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1039a64b6ba800ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the commitment keys DO NOT match, then an error MUST be collected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1039a64b6ba800ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and the next encrypted data key in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b67301d88ef677a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The keyring MUST perform data key unwrapping according to the [Data Key Unwrapping section](#data-key-unwrapping)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0636ca88b9276aaf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the keyring fails to unwrap the data key,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0636ca88b9276aaf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "then an error MUST be collected and the next encrypted data key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0636ca88b9276aaf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a79a007fe40a992",
                  "a2c95399a578ae54"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If the response does satisfy these requirements then OnDecrypt:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "639de104841dc8e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- MUST set the plaintext data key on the [decryption materials](./structures.md#decryption-materials)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "952f03f860976cd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- MUST immediately return the modified [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50d543311e9c44ce",
                  "4ec945b76f315326"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If OnDecrypt fails to successfully decrypt any encrypted data key,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50d543311e9c44ce",
                  "4ec945b76f315326"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "then it MUST yield an error that includes all the collected errors."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "40933d529f002345",
            "40933d529f002345",
            "6c5f3c994525172b",
            "6c5f3c994525172b",
            "6c5f3c994525172b",
            "c83da62f3d6f08bf",
            "c83da62f3d6f08bf",
            "cc47b71496198213",
            "5c9cc251586d8e85",
            "61469b891b3cd1dc",
            "61469b891b3cd1dc",
            "61469b891b3cd1dc",
            "3a0ad97ec2df7165",
            "c84b8d1e2803b373",
            "acc53df814b2f6ba",
            "7b6c33a3c85bf810",
            "c2e1b0a668365823",
            "50be267dcbe5d282",
            "5c34efc99ddc3114",
            "5c34efc99ddc3114",
            "5c34efc99ddc3114",
            "7fded9bc99bd1e5d",
            "7fded9bc99bd1e5d",
            "fc540e0009bd10e5",
            "fc540e0009bd10e5",
            "fc540e0009bd10e5",
            "bbf0b2ee6d77038d",
            "ed7e6781d9170726",
            "4811e577274de98e",
            "181c419b082c7a68",
            "0bc0ba6f326ff103",
            "0bc0ba6f326ff103",
            "cc6f91e8e29029f9",
            "cc6f91e8e29029f9",
            "2dd45a078b58f8d6",
            "2dd45a078b58f8d6",
            "0e96b9ff3aaebd86",
            "0e96b9ff3aaebd86",
            "e93099f56096e2ea",
            "c44be1b73a4232bc",
            "43ed96077249cb2f",
            "43ed96077249cb2f",
            "43ed96077249cb2f",
            "2069003d6011471c",
            "1039a64b6ba800ca",
            "1039a64b6ba800ca",
            "7b67301d88ef677a",
            "0636ca88b9276aaf",
            "0636ca88b9276aaf",
            "0636ca88b9276aaf",
            "639de104841dc8e7",
            "952f03f860976cd4",
            "4ec945b76f315326",
            "4ec945b76f315326"
          ],
          "title": "OnDecrypt"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS ECDH Keyring"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-hierarchical-keyring.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-hierarchical-keyring",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS Hierarchical Keyring"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.1.0"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.1.0",
            "  - Initital record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "The Hierarchical keyring interacts with Amazon DynamoDB (AWS DDB) and AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS).",
            "The Hierarchical keyring uses AWS KMS Keys to protect [Branch Keys](#definitions) to establish a key hierarchy",
            "and it uses Amazon DynamoDB to persist these [Branch Keys](#definitions).",
            "The Hierarchical keyring allows customers to reduce AWS KMS calls by locally caching branch keys in the established hierarchy and using them to protect data keys."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [
            "- [Branch Key(s)](../structures.md#branch-key): Data keys that are reused to derive unique data keys for envelope encryption.",
            "  For security considerations on when to rotate the branch key, refer to [Appendix B](#appendix-b-security-considerations-for-branch-key-rotation).",
            "- [Keystore](../branch-key-store.md): a resource responsible for managing and protecting branch keys in DDB.",
            "- [UUID](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc4122.txt): a universally unique identifier that can be represented as a byte sequence or a string."
          ],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "interface",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "343346f5d6b09db8",
                  "a6511a849b2fc315"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST implement the [AWS Encryption SDK Keyring interface](../keyring-interface.md#interface)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "a6511a849b2fc315"
          ],
          "title": "Interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            "On initialization, the caller:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ec6a8da6ab02930",
                  "758ec723671e9110"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST provide a [Keystore](../branch-key-store.md)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a867c2e777b8ff6",
                  "0a2e10c69bb0b7f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST provide a [cache limit TTL"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a2e10c69bb0b7f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "](#cache-limit-ttl)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a224461f713eb4a5",
                  "a3061b2ad460064b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST provide either a Branch Key Identifier or a [Branch Key Supplier](#branch-key-supplier)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "397464c18c442a44"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "- MAY provide a max cache size"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "77472107f50e7435"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "On initialization the Hierarchical Keyring MUST initialize a [cryptographic-materials-cache](../local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md) with the configured cache limit TTL and the max cache size."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1568b537e455ea53"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If no max cache size is provided, the crypotgraphic materials cache MUST be configured to a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1568b537e455ea53"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "max cache size of 1000."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "758ec723671e9110",
            "0a2e10c69bb0b7f9",
            "a3061b2ad460064b",
            "397464c18c442a44",
            "77472107f50e7435",
            "1568b537e455ea53",
            "1568b537e455ea53"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "cache-limit-ttl",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1f044ece5c379161"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The maximum amount of time in seconds that an entry within the cache may be used before it MUST be evicted."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cee56efaf62194ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The client MUST set a time-to-live (TTL) for [branch key materials](../structures.md#branch-key-materials) in the underlying cache."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "102a617a04c5cb13"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This value MUST be greater than zero."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1f044ece5c379161",
            "cee56efaf62194ca",
            "102a617a04c5cb13"
          ],
          "title": "Cache Limit TTL"
        },
        {
          "id": "structure",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Structure"
        },
        {
          "id": "ciphertext",
          "lines": [
            "This structure is a sequence of bytes in big-endian format to be used as",
            "the [ciphertext](structures.md#ciphertext) field in",
            "[encrypted data keys](structures.md#encrypted-data-key) produced by the AWS KMS Hierarchical Keyring.",
            "",
            "This structure is formed using the 16 byte `salt` used to derive the `derivedBranchKey`",
            "concatenated with the AES-GCM-256 12 byte `IV`",
            "concatenated with the byte representation of the UUID branch key version from the AWS DDB response `version` value",
            "concatenated with the AES Encryption output from the [branch key wrapping](#branch-key-wrapping).",
            "",
            "The following table describes the fields that form the ciphertext for this keyring.",
            "The bytes are appended in the order shown.",
            "",
            "| Field              | Length (bytes) | Interpreted as |",
            "| ------------------ | -------------- | -------------- |",
            "| Salt               | 16             | bytes          |",
            "| IV                 | 12             | bytes          |",
            "| Version            | 16             | bytes          |",
            "| Encrypted Key      | 32             | bytes          |",
            "| Authentication Tag | 16             | bytes          |"
          ],
          "title": "Ciphertext"
        },
        {
          "id": "authentication-tag",
          "lines": [
            "The authentication tag returned by the AES-GCM encryption."
          ],
          "title": "Authentication Tag"
        },
        {
          "id": "operation",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Operation"
        },
        {
          "id": "onencrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fc51d54cf54b3104",
                  "6b0f6dc0477b554f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST take [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "The `branchKeyId` used in this operation is either the configured branchKeyId, if supplied, or the result of the `branchKeySupplier`'s",
            "`getBranchKeyId` operation, using the encryption material's encryption context as input.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ccc9a803067670d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) do not contain a plaintext data key,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ccc9a803067670d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST generate a random plaintext data key, according to the key length defined in the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md#encryption-key-length)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d0ccd0a54ffea6a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The process used to generate this random plaintext data key MUST use a secure source of randomness."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4e762998bdc1b1a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The hierarchical keyring MUST attempt to find [branch key materials](../structures.md#branch-key-materials)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4e762998bdc1b1a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "from the underlying [cryptographic materials cache](../local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66cc8c289633316f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The hierarchical keyring MUST use the formulas specified in [Appendix A](#appendix-a-cache-entry-identifier-formulas)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66cc8c289633316f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "to compute the [cache entry identifier](../cryptographic-materials-cache.md#cache-identifier)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fc4459b01e7a12bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If a cache entry is found and the entry's TTL has not expired, the hierarchical keyring MUST use those branch key materials for key wrapping."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dee15586436c06ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If a cache entry is not found or the cache entry is expired, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "604fb624b552a611",
                  "dee15586436c06ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "the hierarchical keyring MUST attempt to obtain the branch key materials"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "604fb624b552a611",
                  "dee15586436c06ac"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "by querying the backing branch keystore specified in the [retrieve OnEncrypt branch key materials](#query-branch-keystore-onencrypt) section."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90cca074046cdf51"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the keyring is not able to retrieve [branch key materials](../structures.md#branch-key-materials)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90cca074046cdf51"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "through the underlying cryptographic materials cache or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90cca074046cdf51"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "it no longer has access to them through the backing keystore, OnEncrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "Otherwise, OnEncrypt:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ec3e02bc6d617a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- MUST wrap a data key with the branch key materials according to the [branch key wrapping](#branch-key-wrapping) section."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "115447b2957d2c44"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the keyring is unable to wrap a plaintext data key, OnEncrypt MUST fail"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "115447b2957d2c44"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e10fe92ff83c1073"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Otherwise, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b857118313b6c2c",
                  "e10fe92ff83c1073"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST append a new [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b857118313b6c2c",
                  "e10fe92ff83c1073"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "to the encrypted data key list in the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e10fe92ff83c1073"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": ", constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a76641d27bf43097"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52ba5aaa9ae086fe",
                  "a76641d27bf43097"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "[ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext): MUST be serialized as the [hierarchical keyring ciphertext](#ciphertext)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e4a923f639908efa"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48d386e10cf79841",
                  "e4a923f639908efa"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "[key provider id](../structures.md#key-provider-id): MUST be UTF8 Encoded \"aws-kms-hierarchy\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d60ff699c3bc4e78"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7f0508058785b5d2",
                  "d60ff699c3bc4e78"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "[key provider info](../structures.md#key-provider-information): MUST be the UTF8 Encoded AWS DDB response `branch-key-id`"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6b0f6dc0477b554f",
            "6ccc9a803067670d",
            "6ccc9a803067670d",
            "d0ccd0a54ffea6a3",
            "b4e762998bdc1b1a",
            "b4e762998bdc1b1a",
            "66cc8c289633316f",
            "66cc8c289633316f",
            "fc4459b01e7a12bd",
            "dee15586436c06ac",
            "dee15586436c06ac",
            "90cca074046cdf51",
            "90cca074046cdf51",
            "90cca074046cdf51",
            "7ec3e02bc6d617a8",
            "115447b2957d2c44",
            "115447b2957d2c44",
            "e10fe92ff83c1073",
            "e10fe92ff83c1073",
            "a76641d27bf43097",
            "e4a923f639908efa",
            "d60ff699c3bc4e78"
          ],
          "title": "OnEncrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "query-branch-keystore-onencrypt",
          "lines": [
            "The branch keystore persists [branch keys](#definitions) that are reused to derive unique data keys for envelope encryption to",
            "reduce the number of calls to AWS KMS through the use of the",
            "[cryptographic materials cache](../cryptographic-materials-cache.md).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bad476acb562eff2"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST call the Keystore's [GetActiveBranchKey](../branch-key-store.md#getactivebranchkey) operation with the following inputs:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- the `branchKeyId` used in this operation",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e51445048c939f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the Keystore's GetActiveBranchKey operation succeeds"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e51445048c939f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the keyring MUST put the returned branch key materials in the cache using the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e51445048c939f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "formula defined in [Appendix A](#appendix-a-cache-entry-identifier-formulas)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f3e6dd257b00652"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Otherwise, OnEncrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "bad476acb562eff2",
            "3e51445048c939f3",
            "3e51445048c939f3",
            "3e51445048c939f3",
            "6f3e6dd257b00652"
          ],
          "title": "Query Branch Keystore OnEncrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "branch-key-wrapping",
          "lines": [
            "To derive and encrypt a data key the keyring will follow the same key derivation and encryption as [AWS KMS](https://rwc.iacr.org/2018/Slides/Gueron.pdf).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d3ee7d4ff551483",
                  "4e450a062e927546"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The hierarchical keyring MUST:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "1. Generate a 16 byte random `salt` using a secure source of randomness",
            "1. Generate a 12 byte random `IV` using a secure source of randomness",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b85a9d60406a276c"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "1. Use a [KDF in Counter Mode with a Pseudo Random Function with HMAC SHA 256](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-108r1.pdf)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e3d7a1a95bd364e"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "to derive a 32 byte `derivedBranchKey`"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " data key with the following inputs:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0c82557bfd3d31b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "- Use the `salt` as the salt."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43c38199a120a57d"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "- Use the branch key as the `key`."
              }
            ],
            "   - Use the UTF8 Encoded value \"aws-kms-hierarchy\" as the label.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dcb36bf5ddf03416"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "1. Encrypt a plaintext data key with the `derivedBranchKey` using `AES-GCM-256` with the following inputs:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87cd88b8a1675fa5"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e9c87b2e3fb7f066",
                  "87cd88b8a1675fa5"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "MUST use the `derivedBranchKey` as the AES-GCM cipher key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5123f879d842903"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0e8f7b3b2be9726d",
                  "c5123f879d842903"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "MUST use the plain text data key that will be wrapped by the `derivedBranchKey` as the AES-GCM message."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "633de7306fb1a70a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bc526684cd94faf",
                  "633de7306fb1a70a"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "MUST use the derived `IV` as the AES-GCM IV."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e6461b97dc9f5c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "013522315ca0b784",
                  "4e6461b97dc9f5c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST use an authentication tag byte of length 16."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a618cabe0075b1f",
                  "fe9e2bce40bcc8df"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- MUST use the serialized [AAD](#branch-key-wrapping-and-unwrapping-aad) as the AES-GCM AAD."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b974ac55949d794e"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If OnEncrypt fails to do any of the above, OnEncrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4e450a062e927546",
            "87cd88b8a1675fa5",
            "c5123f879d842903",
            "633de7306fb1a70a",
            "4e6461b97dc9f5c8",
            "fe9e2bce40bcc8df",
            "b974ac55949d794e"
          ],
          "title": "Branch Key Wrapping"
        },
        {
          "id": "ondecrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b83f2eb963039df"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST take [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) and a list of [encrypted data keys](../structures.md#encrypted-data-keys) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "The `branchKeyId` used in this operation is either the configured branchKeyId, if supplied, or the result of the `branchKeySupplier`'s",
            "`getBranchKeyId` operation, using the decryption material's encryption context as input.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "529d86ef79914bec"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the decryption materials already contain a `PlainTextDataKey`, OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7958c1e7acba08be"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The set of encrypted data keys MUST first be filtered to match this keyring’s configuration."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " For the encrypted data key to match:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "17d59826022f6a5d",
                  "6fad56ac8bf99ef7"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- Its provider ID MUST match the UTF8 Encoded value of “aws-kms-hierarchy”."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "149c607577794938"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- Deserialize the key provider info, if deserialization fails the next EDK in the set MUST be attempted"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "149c607577794938"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4ecfaafaa73fec0",
                  "7b2ad1238405e646"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The deserialized key provider info MUST be UTF8 Decoded"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b2ad1238405e646"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac2833eea734c214",
                  "7b2ad1238405e646"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "MUST match this keyring's configured `Branch Key Identifier`."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ccbc3662909115ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "For each encrypted data key in the filtered set, one at a time, OnDecrypt MUST attempt to decrypt the encrypted data key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "42524b96a3eeaafd"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If this attempt results in an error, then these errors MUST be collected."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df76b1914dacc746"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "To decrypt each encrypted data key in the filtered set, the hierarchical keyring MUST attempt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df76b1914dacc746"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "to find the corresponding [branch key materials](../structures.md#branch-key-materials)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df76b1914dacc746"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "from the underlying [cryptographic materials cache](../local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0bf8d7c300bdd708"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The hierarchical keyring MUST use the OnDecrypt formula specified in [Appendix A](#decryption-materials)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0bf8d7c300bdd708"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "in order to compute the [cache entry identifier](cryptographic-materials-cache.md#cache-identifier)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d334038903fa0557"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If a cache entry is found and the entry's TTL has not expired, the hierarchical keyring MUST use those branch key materials for key unwrapping."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "761a0dbf7b777a8c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If a cache entry is not found or the cache entry is expired, the hierarchical keyring"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "761a0dbf7b777a8c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "MUST attempt to obtain the branch key materials by calling the backing branch key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "761a0dbf7b777a8c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "store specified in the [retrieve OnDecrypt branch key materials](#getitem-branch-keystore-ondecrypt) section."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2970640ac5f7b39b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the keyring is not able to retrieve `branch key materials` from the backing keystore then OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "If the keyring is able to retrieve `branch key materials` from the backing keystore, OnDecrypt:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd84610295b31689"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- MUST unwrap the encrypted data key with the branch key materials according to the [branch key unwrapping](#branch-key-unwrapping) section."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "261bb696287afd58",
                  "94357759304b34fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "If a decryption succeeds, this keyring MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "261bb696287afd58",
                  "94357759304b34fe"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "add the resulting plaintext data key to the decryption materials and return the modified materials."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1809b05856e7cd24"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If OnDecrypt fails to successfully decrypt any [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1809b05856e7cd24"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "then it MUST yield an error that includes all the collected errors"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1809b05856e7cd24"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2b83f2eb963039df",
            "529d86ef79914bec",
            "7958c1e7acba08be",
            "6fad56ac8bf99ef7",
            "149c607577794938",
            "7b2ad1238405e646",
            "ccbc3662909115ff",
            "42524b96a3eeaafd",
            "df76b1914dacc746",
            "df76b1914dacc746",
            "df76b1914dacc746",
            "0bf8d7c300bdd708",
            "0bf8d7c300bdd708",
            "d334038903fa0557",
            "761a0dbf7b777a8c",
            "761a0dbf7b777a8c",
            "761a0dbf7b777a8c",
            "2970640ac5f7b39b",
            "cd84610295b31689",
            "94357759304b34fe",
            "94357759304b34fe",
            "1809b05856e7cd24",
            "1809b05856e7cd24",
            "1809b05856e7cd24"
          ],
          "title": "OnDecrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "getitem-branch-keystore-ondecrypt",
          "lines": [
            "The branch keystore persists [branch keys](#definitions) that are reused to derive unique data keys for key wrapping to",
            "reduce the number of calls to AWS KMS through the use of the",
            "[cryptographic materials cache](../cryptographic-materials-cache.md).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b793921d5920549"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST calculate the following values:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- Deserialize the UTF8-Decoded `branch-key-id` from the [key provider info](../structures.md#key-provider-information) of the [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key)",
            "  and verify this is equal to the configured or supplied `branch-key-id`.",
            "- Deserialize the UUID string representation of the `version` from the [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) [ciphertext](#ciphertext).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b538c7e27fd5706"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST call the Keystore's [GetBranchKeyVersion](../branch-key-store.md#getbranchkeyversion) operation with the following inputs:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- The deserialized, UTF8-Decoded `branch-key-id`",
            "- The deserialized UUID string representation of the `version`",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b3bc6a8a0958d64"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the Keystore's GetBranchKeyVersion operation succeeds"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b3bc6a8a0958d64"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the keyring MUST put the returned branch key materials in the cache using the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b3bc6a8a0958d64"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "formula defined in [Appendix A](#appendix-a-cache-entry-identifier-formulas)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b8716c6d94c23cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Otherwise, OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9b793921d5920549",
            "5b538c7e27fd5706",
            "7b3bc6a8a0958d64",
            "7b3bc6a8a0958d64",
            "7b3bc6a8a0958d64",
            "3b8716c6d94c23cf"
          ],
          "title": "GetItem Branch Keystore OnDecrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "branch-key-unwrapping",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "067fb3590836beb9"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "To decrypt an encrypted data key with a branch key, the hierarchical keyring MUST:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "1. Deserialize the 16 byte random `salt` from the [edk ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext).",
            "1. Deserialize the 12 byte random `IV` from the [edk ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext).",
            "1. Deserialize the 16 byte `version` from the [edk ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext).",
            "1. Deserialize the `encrypted key` from the [edk ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext).",
            "1. Deserialize the `authentication tag` from the [edk ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext).",
            "",
            "1. Use a [KDF in Counter Mode with a Pseudo Random Function with HMAC SHA 256](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-108r1.pdf) to derive",
            "   the 32 byte `derivedBranchKey` data key with the following inputs:",
            "   - Use the `salt` as the salt.",
            "   - Use the branch key as the `key`.",
            "1. Decrypt the encrypted data key with the `derivedBranchKey` using `AES-GCM-256` with the following inputs:",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9229218c321069f6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- It MUST use the `encrypted key` obtained from deserialization as the AES-GCM input ciphertext."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0eeb4f08cae7e314"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- It MUST use the `authentication tag` obtained from deserialization as the AES-GCM input authentication tag."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87a0fb4647001e25"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- It MUST use the `derivedBranchKey` as the AES-GCM cipher key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e187c93d42b33c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- It MUST use the `IV` obtained from deserialization as the AES-GCM input IV."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e78a0be5c79e96b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- It MUST use the serialized [encryption context](#branch-key-wrapping-and-unwrapping-aad) as the AES-GCM AAD."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "74cb536b006decc1"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If OnDecrypt fails to do any of the above, OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "067fb3590836beb9",
            "9229218c321069f6",
            "0eeb4f08cae7e314",
            "87a0fb4647001e25",
            "4e187c93d42b33c6",
            "e78a0be5c79e96b8",
            "74cb536b006decc1"
          ],
          "title": "Branch Key Unwrapping"
        },
        {
          "id": "branch-key-wrapping-and-unwrapping-aad",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "02f8a45abd792f14",
                  "0e456624171ba976"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "To Encrypt and Decrypt the `wrappedDerivedBranchKey` the keyring MUST include the following values as part of the AAD for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "02f8a45abd792f14",
                  "0e456624171ba976"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "the AES Encrypt/Decrypt calls."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4570ef622c95afe5",
                  "fc5ab1629e09e3c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "To construct the AAD, the keyring MUST concatenate the following values"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "1. \"aws-kms-hierarchy\" as UTF8 Bytes",
            "1. Value of `branch-key-id` as UTF8 Bytes",
            "1. [version](../structures.md#branch-key-version) as Bytes",
            "1. [encryption context](structures.md#encryption-context-1) from the input",
            "   [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) according to the [encryption context serialization specification](../structures.md#serialization).",
            "",
            "| Field               | Length (bytes) | Interpreted as                                       |",
            "| ------------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |",
            "| \"aws-kms-hierarchy\" | 17             | UTF-8 Encoded                                        |",
            "| branch-key-id       | Variable       | UTF-8 Encoded                                        |",
            "| version             | 16             | Bytes                                                |",
            "| encryption context  | Variable       | [Encryption Context](../structures.md#serialization) |",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e2ee853963a59424"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the keyring cannot serialize the encryption context, the operation MUST fail."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "0e456624171ba976",
            "0e456624171ba976",
            "fc5ab1629e09e3c6",
            "e2ee853963a59424"
          ],
          "title": "Branch Key Wrapping and Unwrapping AAD"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-a-cache-entry-identifier-formulas",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06e92a8686323683"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "When accessing the underlying cryptographic materials cache,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06e92a8686323683"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the hierarchical keyring MUST use the formulas specified in this appendix"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06e92a8686323683"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "in order to compute the [cache entry identifier](../cryptographic-materials-cache.md#cache-identifier)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "06e92a8686323683",
            "06e92a8686323683",
            "06e92a8686323683"
          ],
          "title": "Appendix A: Cache Entry Identifier Formulas"
        },
        {
          "id": "preliminaries",
          "lines": [
            "Each of the cache entry identifier formulas includes serialized information related to the branch key,",
            "as defined in the [Key Provider Info](../structures.md#key-provider-information)."
          ],
          "title": "Preliminaries"
        },
        {
          "id": "encryption-materials",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b282530cffe9363a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "When the hierarchical keyring receives an OnEncrypt request,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b282530cffe9363a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the cache entry identifier MUST be calculated as the first 32 bytes of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b282530cffe9363a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "SHA-512 hash of the following byte strings, in the order listed:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "| Field                    | Length (bytes) | Interpreted as |",
            "| ------------------------ | -------------- | -------------- |",
            "| Length of branch-key-id  | 3              | UInt8          |",
            "| branch-key-id            | Variable       | UTF-8 Encoded  |",
            "| Null Byte                | 1              | `0x00`         |",
            "| Constant string \"ACTIVE\" | 6              | UTF-8 Encoded  |",
            "",
            "As a formula:",
            "",
            "```",
            "branch-key-id = UTF8Encode(hierarchicalKeyring.BranchKeyIdentifier)",
            "branch-key-digest - SHA512(branch-key-id)",
            "",
            "ENTRY_ID = SHA512(",
            "    LengthUint8(branch-key-id) +",
            "    branch-key-digest +",
            "    + 0x00",
            "    + UTF8Encode(\"ACTIVE\")",
            ")[0:32]",
            "```"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b282530cffe9363a",
            "b282530cffe9363a",
            "b282530cffe9363a"
          ],
          "title": "Encryption Materials"
        },
        {
          "id": "decryption-materials",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "558cf99410570caa"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "When the hierarchical keyring receives an OnDecrypt request,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "558cf99410570caa"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "it MUST calculate the cache entry identifier as the first 32 bytes of the SHA-512 hash of the following byte strings, in the order listed:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "| Field                   | Length (bytes) | Interpreted as |",
            "| ----------------------- | -------------- | -------------- |",
            "| Length of branch-key-id | 3              | UInt8          |",
            "| branch-key-id           | Variable       | UTF-8 Encoded  |",
            "| Null Byte               | 1              | `0x00`         |",
            "| Branch key version      | 36             | String         |",
            "",
            "```",
            "branch-key-id = UTF8Encode(edk.providerInfo)",
            "branch-key-digest - SHA512(branch-key-id)",
            "",
            "ENTRY_ID = SHA512(",
            "    LengthUint8(branch-key-id) +",
            "    branch-key-digest +",
            "    0x00 +",
            "    branch key version",
            ")[0:32]",
            "```"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "558cf99410570caa",
            "558cf99410570caa"
          ],
          "title": "Decryption Materials"
        },
        {
          "id": "branch-key-supplier",
          "lines": [
            "The Branch Key Supplier is an interface containing the `GetBranchKeyId` operation.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b125bd03ffe4d86c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This operation MUST take in an encryption context as input,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b125bd03ffe4d86c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "and return a branch key id (string) as output."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "This supplier may be implemented by customers in order to configure behavior where the hierarchical",
            "keyring may decide on which branch key to use based on information in the encryption context.",
            "This gives customers more flexibility in multi-tenant use cases."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b125bd03ffe4d86c",
            "b125bd03ffe4d86c"
          ],
          "title": "Branch Key Supplier"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-b-security-considerations-for-branch-key-rotation",
          "lines": [
            "Branch Keys are not used to wrap plaintext data keys; instead they are used to derive unique `derivedBranchKeys`.",
            "The `derivedBranchKeys` are responsible for wrapping plaintext data keys set on the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials).",
            "",
            "Branch Keys have a limit on how many times they are able to derive a `derivedBranchKey` before a theoretical collision.",
            "",
            "To derive a `derivedBranchKey` the Keyring uses a 16 byte salt for the KDF.",
            "Additionally the keyring uses a 12-byte IV for the AES-GCM-256 for key wrapping.",
            "We have selected to use these `salt` and `IV` parameters as they are the same parameters used",
            "in [AWS KMS key derivation](https://rwc.iacr.org/2018/Slides/Gueron.pdf).",
            "",
            "Overall this results in 28-bytes of randomness.",
            "",
            "Birthday Problem calculations for current selection:",
            "",
            "```",
            "16 + 12 = 28-bytes or 224-bits of randomness",
            "",
            "(224 - 32) / 2 = 96",
            "",
            "2^96 = 7.9228163e+28 or 79,228,162,514,264,337,593,543,950,336",
            "```",
            "",
            "The above number is how many times one would have to wrap with the `derivedBranchKey` before a theoretical collision.",
            "Given the magnitude of the result; it is recommended to rotate the `branchKey` once per year as this is also the cadence",
            "at which AWS KMS rotates its [AWS Managed Keys](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/rotate-keys.html#rotate-keys-how-it-works).",
            "Using this combination of IV and salt for the KDF and Wrapping operations significantly extends the lifetime of the key; this allows",
            "customers to define their rotation schedule by criteria other than cryptographic safety limits."
          ],
          "title": "Appendix B: Security Considerations for Branch Key Rotation"
        },
        {
          "id": "other-considerations",
          "lines": [
            "We considered deriving a `derivedBranchKey` with the following construction.",
            "",
            "Use a 32-byte salt for an HKDF operation using the `branchKey` as the input key material.",
            "Use no IV for AES GCM 256 Key Wrapping",
            "",
            "This would result in a total of 256 bits of randomness",
            "",
            "32 = 256 bits of randomness",
            "",
            "Birthday Problem calculations:",
            "",
            "```",
            "(256 - 32) / 2 = 112",
            "",
            "2^112 = 5,192,296,858,534,827,628,530,496,329,220,096",
            "```",
            "",
            "The above number is how many times one would have to wrap with the `derivedBranchKey` before a theoretical collision.",
            "Although this is a higher number we decided on the current selection of including a salt and an IV to not only",
            "lower the overhead of bytes we have to store in the [edk ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext) but to",
            "easily reason about the security properties of the key derivation since it is what AWS KMS does."
          ],
          "title": "Other considerations"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS Hierarchical Keyring"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-key-arn.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-key-arn",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS Key ARN"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.2.2"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "AWS KMS Key ARNs generally follow [AWS ARN](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/aws-arns-and-namespaces.html))",
            "but there are a few subtle differences.",
            "This is NOT the authoritative source for these rules,",
            "it is just a specification for how the ESDK processes AWS KMS CMK ARNs."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "a-valid-aws-kms-arn",
          "lines": [
            "A string with 5 `:` that delimit following 6 parts:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "1. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f008a2d74a79110e",
                  "6ed9fd190b1c8bfd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST start with string `arn`"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "2. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d53d218f20466d59",
                  "15a9250794fb8412"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The partition MUST be a non-empty"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "3. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "647c2fac1d68a322",
                  "0928e757a7cf3340"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The service MUST be the string `kms`"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "4. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52a0798674ba0c03",
                  "59474422c5dabc49"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The region MUST be a non-empty string"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "5. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e32bab7038651cb",
                  "b4ed2a04de9580e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The account MUST be a non-empty string"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "6. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79d12be94756fdb3",
                  "27b472f9e7fff478"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The resource section MUST be non-empty and MUST be split by a single `/`"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79d12be94756fdb3",
                  "27b472f9e7fff478"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "any additional `/` are included in the resource id"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   1. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e26ad7114e003ca4",
                  "7261f445b1b7fe64"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The resource type MUST be either `alias` or `key`"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   2. "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "712939867a771939",
                  "c401126f2d5f13e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The resource id MUST be a non-empty string"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6ed9fd190b1c8bfd",
            "15a9250794fb8412",
            "0928e757a7cf3340",
            "59474422c5dabc49",
            "b4ed2a04de9580e6",
            "27b472f9e7fff478",
            "27b472f9e7fff478",
            "7261f445b1b7fe64",
            "c401126f2d5f13e7"
          ],
          "title": "A valid AWS KMS ARN"
        },
        {
          "id": "a-valid-aws-kms-identifier",
          "lines": [
            "An AWS KMS identifer can be any of the following",
            "",
            "- A valid AWS KMS ARN",
            "- AWS KMS alias, the resource section of an AWS KMS alias ARN",
            "- AWS KMS key id, the resource id of an AWS KMS key ARN"
          ],
          "title": "A valid AWS KMS identifier"
        },
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-multi-region-keys",
          "lines": [
            "AWS KMS multi-Region keys can be distinguished from a single-Region key because the key id begins with `mrk-`.",
            "AWS KMS MRK aware components can take as input any AWS KMS identifier:",
            "",
            "- AWS KMS key ARN (`arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:2222222222222:key/1234abcd-12ab-34cd-56ef-1234567890ab`)",
            "- AWS KMS multi-Region key ARN (`arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:2222222222222:key/mrk-4321abcd12ab34cd56ef1234567890ab`)",
            "- AWS KMS alias ARN (`arn:aws:kms:us-west-2:111122223333:alias/test-key`)",
            "- AWS KMS key id (`1234abcd-12ab-34cd-56ef-1234567890ab`)",
            "- AWS KMS multi-Region key id (`mrk-4321abcd12ab34cd56ef1234567890ab`)",
            "- AWS KMS alias (`alias/test-key`)",
            "",
            "Since the alias is can be any string a customer can create an alias that started with `mrk-`.",
            "But an alias is not a multi-Region key."
          ],
          "title": "AWS KMS multi-Region keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "identifying-an-an-aws-kms-multi-region-arn",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f468abcaac374d",
                  "22892e984fdd2b2f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This function MUST take a single AWS KMS ARN"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f468abcaac374d",
                  "d9c493d71ae471c0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input is an invalid AWS KMS ARN this function MUST error."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4a47e10d85ee4d0",
                  "e644d1870810c292"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If resource type is “alias”,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4a47e10d85ee4d0",
                  "e644d1870810c292"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this is an AWS KMS alias ARN and MUST return false."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b2fa82015b72036",
                  "53d9d3cbb75d55d4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If resource type is “key” and resource ID starts with “mrk-“,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b2fa82015b72036",
                  "53d9d3cbb75d55d4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this is a AWS KMS multi-Region key ARN and MUST return true."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a44db08fea783451",
                  "96faf81a0e78a072"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If resource type is “key” and resource ID does not start with “mrk-“,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a44db08fea783451",
                  "96faf81a0e78a072"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this is a (single-region) AWS KMS key ARN and MUST return false."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "22892e984fdd2b2f",
            "d9c493d71ae471c0",
            "e644d1870810c292",
            "e644d1870810c292",
            "53d9d3cbb75d55d4",
            "53d9d3cbb75d55d4",
            "96faf81a0e78a072",
            "96faf81a0e78a072"
          ],
          "title": "Identifying an an AWS KMS multi-Region ARN"
        },
        {
          "id": "identifying-an-an-aws-kms-multi-region-identifier",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4416e071cd267c48",
                  "2a46aaf5e115aafa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This function MUST take a single AWS KMS identifier"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e4ab364c1e06460",
                  "bb3929025a58317d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input starts with \"arn:\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e4ab364c1e06460",
                  "bb3929025a58317d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this MUST return the output of [identifying an an AWS KMS multi-Region ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#identifying-an-an-aws-kms-multi-region-arn)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e4ab364c1e06460",
                  "bb3929025a58317d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "called with this input."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bfd73c45641ac347",
                  "91e11a82f4d82e16"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input starts with “alias/“,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bfd73c45641ac347",
                  "91e11a82f4d82e16"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this an AWS KMS alias and not a multi-Region key id and MUST return false."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bfac8bd5d2871121",
                  "a3c8b6160fcdb231"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input starts with “mrk-“,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bfac8bd5d2871121",
                  "a3c8b6160fcdb231"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this is a multi-Region key id and MUST return true."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5ff1e970181aa03",
                  "6e758f791639b6f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input does not start with any of the above,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a5ff1e970181aa03",
                  "6e758f791639b6f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this is not a multi-Region key id and MUST return false."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2a46aaf5e115aafa",
            "bb3929025a58317d",
            "bb3929025a58317d",
            "bb3929025a58317d",
            "91e11a82f4d82e16",
            "91e11a82f4d82e16",
            "a3c8b6160fcdb231",
            "a3c8b6160fcdb231",
            "6e758f791639b6f9",
            "6e758f791639b6f9"
          ],
          "title": "Identifying an an AWS KMS multi-Region identifier"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS Key ARN"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-keyring.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-keyring",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS Keyring"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.3.0"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.3.0",
            "",
            "  - Incorporate [KMS Keyring Redesign](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/tree/master/proposals/2020-07-01_aws-kms-keyring-redesign)",
            "",
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Rename Key IDs to Key Names for increased clarity",
            "  - Update Key Names and Generator sections to reinforce support for all AWS KMS key identifiers",
            "  - [Pull request link for discussions](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/pull/123)",
            "",
            "- 0.2.1",
            "",
            "  - [Clarify naming of KMS to AWS KMS](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-specification/issues/67)",
            "",
            "- 0.2.0",
            "",
            "  - [Remove Keyring Trace](../../changes/2020-05-13_remove-keyring-trace/change.md)",
            "",
            "- 0.1.0-preview",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "A keyring which interacts with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) to create, encrypt, and decrypt data keys",
            "using AWS KMS keys."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "interface",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "324403be59f246a7",
                  "318c78a179c8a389"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST implement the [AWS Encryption SDK Keyring interface](../keyring-interface.md#interface)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "318c78a179c8a389"
          ],
          "title": "Interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            "On initialization, the caller:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b3baed1a9e169bc9",
                  "8a87d2b14314202b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST provide an AWS KMS key identifier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "894bad3e1cc7c06c",
                  "1616a280127f9284"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST provide an AWS KMS SDK client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d8892eb84c69f47e",
                  "e70e95991a6eff76"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "- MAY provide a list of Grant Tokens"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11e879bd83f00cdb",
                  "b36f16489994ed8b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The AWS KMS key identifier MUST NOT be null or empty."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "76a037bb8c5ec9b9",
                  "b243db8c0c4a1539"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The AWS KMS key identifier MUST be [a valid identifier](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-identifier)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be2515b38f639cb5",
                  "d80c054442f4bbda"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The AWS KMS SDK client MUST NOT be null."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8a87d2b14314202b",
            "1616a280127f9284",
            "e70e95991a6eff76",
            "b36f16489994ed8b",
            "b243db8c0c4a1539",
            "d80c054442f4bbda"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "onencrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "64527acb8a31e337",
                  "3b34162c220e799f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST take [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fabe25a5dc175327",
                  "fe0ac710631b7909"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) do not contain a plaintext data key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fabe25a5dc175327",
                  "fe0ac710631b7909"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST attempt to generate a new plaintext data key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fabe25a5dc175327",
                  "fe0ac710631b7909"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "by calling [AWS KMS GenerateDataKey](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_GenerateDataKey.html)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bfec29219099a2f1",
                  "45dd5c0a323bd7b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the keyring calls AWS KMS GenerateDataKeys, it MUST use the configured AWS KMS client to make the call."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da629ba50615195b",
                  "a2d964724c763dd1"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The keyring MUST call AWS KMS GenerateDataKeys with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "27805b89412141ec",
                  "aa01b4b073133a67"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `KeyId` MUST be the keyring's KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3fdb2cbb9aacb29",
                  "321cb4553d04dbbe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `NumberOfBytes` MUST be the [key derivation input length](../algorithm-suites.md#key-derivation-input-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3fdb2cbb9aacb29",
                  "321cb4553d04dbbe"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "specified by the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md) included in the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "efa0d11ba87b34c2",
                  "7829668dcaf21565",
                  "69247f424960d0d7"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "- `EncryptionContext` MUST be the [encryption context](../structures.md#encryption-context)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "efa0d11ba87b34c2",
                  "7829668dcaf21565",
                  "69247f424960d0d7"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "included in the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f2fc0fd5b4c1db7",
                  "9fe1603979d4d4b2",
                  "f5ae32f3220d03c6"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "- `GrantTokens` MUST be this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75acd5f20607ab30",
                  "0759c1f641fc1b07"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the call to [AWS KMS GenerateDataKey](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_GenerateDataKey.html) does not succeed,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "75acd5f20607ab30",
                  "0759c1f641fc1b07"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST NOT modify the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) and MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b0604df0ae8326b",
                  "79bc4c651b4fe46e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the Generate Data Key call succeeds, OnEncrypt MUST verify that the response `Plaintext` length matches"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b0604df0ae8326b",
                  "79bc4c651b4fe46e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the specification of the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md)'s Key Derivation Input Length field."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abab77d5c11d0100",
                  "3326f705d7af590c"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The Generate Data Key response’s `KeyId` MUST be [a valid AWS KMS key ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn)."
              }
            ],
            "If verified, OnEncrypt:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c695f75ab61d6e75"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- MUST set the plaintext data key on the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) as the response `Plaintext`."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "20120c359545acc1",
                  "84e7646a8e789fe7"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- MUST append a new [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) to the encrypted data key list in the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials), constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4470883d9990caf3",
                  "3af1c499c0a070e4"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- the [ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext) MUST be the response `CiphertextBlob`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b3ffa67560e17ac",
                  "d8f1632e431db569"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- the [key provider id](../structures.md#key-provider-id) MUST be \"aws-kms\"."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "55e8916b9de2373f",
                  "84e203a0fb9ae9ff"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- the [key provider information](../structures.md#key-provider-information) MUST be the response `KeyId`."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6ed672acdf38878",
                  "18323836371b5a44"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST output the modified [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d84b3d3fbfdf9357",
                  "ac7c26086f0a3982"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) do contain a plaintext data key,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d84b3d3fbfdf9357",
                  "ac7c26086f0a3982"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST attempt to encrypt the plaintext data key using the configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "defc7956a7dcd14a",
                  "cc775498dd9e8b20"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The keyring MUST call [AWS KMS Encrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Encrypt.html) using the configured AWS KMS client."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2ceb4b3868f5671d",
                  "93c97f309fccf833"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The keyring MUST AWS KMS Encrypt call with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b7aa4d0cdb127d5",
                  "9cf422f114cc3fd5"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `KeyId` MUST be the configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "82552b3fcd1cd7e9",
                  "5295df4915441838"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `PlaintextDataKey` MUST be the plaintext data key in the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "- `EncryptionContext` MUST be the [encryption context](../structures.md#encryption-context) included in the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials).",
            "- `GrantTokens` MUST be this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fad9e814aa8e49ff",
                  "d3eb4da0e07097a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the call to [AWS KMS Encrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Encrypt.html) does not succeed, OnEncrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ddb07d8af31d3db8",
                  "03875f36c8e8185e"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the Encrypt call succeeds the response’s `KeyId` MUST be [A valid AWS KMS key ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "268f25d77f495a2e",
                  "5151c4a67e5366b7"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If verified, OnEncrypt MUST append a new [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) to the encrypted data key list in the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials), constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e27f5f2eeefe3de1"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The [ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext) MUST be the response `CiphertextBlob`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "42dc25da1589418a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The [key provider id](../structures.md#key-provider-id) MUST be \"aws-kms\"."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd88e3d05321e31c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The [key provider information](../structures.md#key-provider-information) MUST be the response `KeyId`."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " Note that the `KeyId` in the response is always in key ARN format."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "41a4a9020ff82b34",
                  "b804282526bd1bcd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If all Encrypt calls succeed, OnEncrypt MUST output the modified [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "3b34162c220e799f",
            "fe0ac710631b7909",
            "fe0ac710631b7909",
            "fe0ac710631b7909",
            "45dd5c0a323bd7b2",
            "a2d964724c763dd1",
            "aa01b4b073133a67",
            "321cb4553d04dbbe",
            "321cb4553d04dbbe",
            "69247f424960d0d7",
            "69247f424960d0d7",
            "f5ae32f3220d03c6",
            "0759c1f641fc1b07",
            "0759c1f641fc1b07",
            "79bc4c651b4fe46e",
            "79bc4c651b4fe46e",
            "3326f705d7af590c",
            "c695f75ab61d6e75",
            "84e7646a8e789fe7",
            "3af1c499c0a070e4",
            "d8f1632e431db569",
            "84e203a0fb9ae9ff",
            "18323836371b5a44",
            "ac7c26086f0a3982",
            "ac7c26086f0a3982",
            "cc775498dd9e8b20",
            "93c97f309fccf833",
            "9cf422f114cc3fd5",
            "5295df4915441838",
            "d3eb4da0e07097a6",
            "03875f36c8e8185e",
            "5151c4a67e5366b7",
            "e27f5f2eeefe3de1",
            "42dc25da1589418a",
            "cd88e3d05321e31c",
            "b804282526bd1bcd"
          ],
          "title": "OnEncrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "ondecrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7c8dbea2d882f242",
                  "13b6fe47d653744f",
                  "6abf196987c489cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST take [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7c8dbea2d882f242",
                  "13b6fe47d653744f",
                  "6abf196987c489cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "a list of [encrypted data keys](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bdb3139ea657ee10",
                  "4485b3945664d5a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) already contained a valid plaintext data key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bdb3139ea657ee10",
                  "4485b3945664d5a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST return an error."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "db01c6243249b3d4",
                  "234f2b82e0c58830"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The set of encrypted data keys MUST first be filtered to match this keyring’s configuration."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " For the encrypted data key to match:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52219b7652e1c986",
                  "fd5ead4c702c742a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- Its provider ID MUST exactly match the value “aws-kms”."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "116be25bc066c3b4",
                  "5d32f0e76c8f4837"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The provider info MUST be a [valid AWS KMS ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn) with a resource type of `key` or OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "456325f6cc77e232",
                  "b14f3ea367a01c45"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The provider info MUST match the configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d24983f655090261",
                  "a7c267bce22f3aee"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "For each encrypted data key in the filtered set, one at a time, the OnDecrypt MUST attempt to decrypt the data key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d24983f655090261",
                  "26d1fbf0863302c7"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If this attempt results in an error, then these errors MUST be collected."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "40afb12dbcbe9cfd",
                  "95f46867e6de2e31"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "To attempt to decrypt a particular [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "40afb12dbcbe9cfd",
                  "95f46867e6de2e31"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST call [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) with the configured AWS KMS client."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1ef6fa570bbab637",
                  "0b9a026fad741078"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "When calling [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html), the keyring MUST call with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c99145292f77be91",
                  "b1065f43933da635"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `KeyId` MUST be the configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf5da748229573dd",
                  "86591d546de8b593"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `CiphertextBlob` MUST be the [encrypted data key ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b8e7a5f398ff2929",
                  "54d5dd0f801d2030"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `EncryptionContext` MUST be the [encryption context](../structures.md#encryption-context) included in the input [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ed67328ce234d3bf",
                  "6e398bd3b50c32ae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- `GrantTokens` MUST be this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "If the call to [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) succeeds, OnDecrypt verifies:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be5091c3c792e5c7",
                  "afe603996577becb"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- The `KeyId` field in the response MUST equal the configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8960560255e70c7",
                  "1c99c8e9797586c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- The length of the response’s `Plaintext` MUST equal the [key derivation input length](../algorithm-suites.md#key-derivation-input-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8960560255e70c7",
                  "1c99c8e9797586c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "specified by the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md) included in the input [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1cf1bc5125548b1b",
                  "91797cdc730adfc9"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the response does not satisfies these requirements then an error MUST be collected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1cf1bc5125548b1b",
                  "91797cdc730adfc9"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "and the next encrypted data key in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "If the response does satisfy these requirements then OnDecrypt:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72bdcbbc3e17bcb1",
                  "3d2474b8e1fae46d"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- MUST set the plaintext data key on the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) as the response `Plaintext`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a79494a8b2786824",
                  "3208afd2a5d46422"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- MUST immediately return the modified [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "016693b589f75a32",
                  "a67ff36fa06edac4",
                  "60e9ab52c6d6a828"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If OnDecrypt fails to successfully decrypt any [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "016693b589f75a32",
                  "a67ff36fa06edac4",
                  "60e9ab52c6d6a828"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "then it MUST yield an error that includes all the collected errors."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6abf196987c489cc",
            "6abf196987c489cc",
            "4485b3945664d5a8",
            "4485b3945664d5a8",
            "234f2b82e0c58830",
            "fd5ead4c702c742a",
            "5d32f0e76c8f4837",
            "b14f3ea367a01c45",
            "a7c267bce22f3aee",
            "26d1fbf0863302c7",
            "95f46867e6de2e31",
            "95f46867e6de2e31",
            "0b9a026fad741078",
            "b1065f43933da635",
            "86591d546de8b593",
            "54d5dd0f801d2030",
            "6e398bd3b50c32ae",
            "afe603996577becb",
            "1c99c8e9797586c8",
            "1c99c8e9797586c8",
            "91797cdc730adfc9",
            "91797cdc730adfc9",
            "3d2474b8e1fae46d",
            "3208afd2a5d46422",
            "60e9ab52c6d6a828",
            "60e9ab52c6d6a828"
          ],
          "title": "OnDecrypt"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS Keyring"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-mrk-are-unique.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "assert-aws-kms-mrk-are-unique",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Assert AWS KMS MRK are unique"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.2.2"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "Duplicate multi-region key ids create ambiguity about which Region to contact.",
            "This is better resolved outside of the AWS Encryption SDK.",
            "While preferring the \"local\" Region is a seductive solution,",
            "this can not be 100% correct.",
            "First, because not all code runs in an AWS Region,",
            "and second because customers may want create privacy controls around their data.",
            "In this case nearby region may exists and store ciphertext,",
            "but may be restricted from having the AWS KMS keys.",
            "In any complicated deployment determining the closest,",
            "or preferred region is itself a complicated task.",
            "It will be easier for customers to reason about this criteria",
            "and ensure their code is correct",
            "if the AWS Encryption SDK offers one and only one configuration for a behavior.",
            "e.g. If the preferred region logic results in an ambiguous configuration",
            "is informed and they can resolve the ambiguity.",
            "Rather than attempting to resolve it ourselves.",
            "",
            "Preferring the local region does not suffice:",
            "not all code runs in an AWS Region boundary,",
            "and customers need to assert intentions to use a region."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementation",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3bbf6d6e4ba34e42",
                  "9753810bb47bf361"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The caller MUST provide:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- A list of AWS KMS key identifiers",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d70b39701e8716c9",
                  "b73be6ca5dce650f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the list does not contain any [multi-Region keys](aws-kms-key-arn.md#identifying-an-aws-kms-multi-region-key)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d70b39701e8716c9",
                  "b73be6ca5dce650f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this function MUST exit successfully."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "78a52e9d67e2e614",
                  "cf0d16e1ba8a8091"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If there are zero duplicate resource ids between the multi-region keys,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "78a52e9d67e2e614",
                  "cf0d16e1ba8a8091"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this function MUST exit successfully"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6e26e809222891",
                  "7965714a062cb0ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If any duplicate multi-region resource ids exist,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6e26e809222891",
                  "7965714a062cb0ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "this function MUST yield an error"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6e26e809222891",
                  "7965714a062cb0ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "that includes all identifiers with duplicate resource ids"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6e26e809222891",
                  "7965714a062cb0ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "not only the first duplicate found."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9753810bb47bf361",
            "b73be6ca5dce650f",
            "b73be6ca5dce650f",
            "cf0d16e1ba8a8091",
            "cf0d16e1ba8a8091",
            "7965714a062cb0ef",
            "7965714a062cb0ef",
            "7965714a062cb0ef",
            "7965714a062cb0ef"
          ],
          "title": "Implementation"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Assert AWS KMS MRK are unique"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key-provider.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key-provider",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS MRK Aware Master Key Provider"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.2.2"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "A Master Key Provider which interacts with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)",
            "to create, encrypt, and decrypt data keys",
            "using AWS KMS defined Customer Master Keys (CMKs)."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "interface",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ace234bafbe72956",
                  "f834d5354872d849"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "MUST implement the [Master Key Provider Interface](../master-key-provider-interface.md#interface)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f834d5354872d849"
          ],
          "title": "Interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "8aaa9dfe00d17d0a"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "On initialization the caller MUST provide:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- An indicator of either strict or discovery mode e.g an. `isDiscovery` boolean"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- A list of AWS KMS key identifiers, the list may be empty"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- An optional list of AWS KMS grant tokens"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- A method that can take a region string and return an AWS KMS client e.g. a regional client supplier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- An optional discovery filter that is an AWS partition and a set of AWS accounts"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- An optional discovery MRK Region string"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "005917faeff76e97"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The key id list MUST NOT be empty or null in strict mode."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "290a1f8b684c1e79"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The key id list MUST NOT contain any null or empty string values."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "2baaab08670dec9a"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "All AWS KMS key identifiers are be passed to [Assert AWS KMS MRK are unique](aws-kms-mrk-are-unique.md#Implementation)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "2baaab08670dec9a"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "and the function MUST return success."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "21544912b120ab9e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "A discovery filter MUST NOT be configured in strict mode."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "db11024267fe1cd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "A default MRK Region MUST NOT be configured in strict mode."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "665997fcb0937a6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "In discovery mode if a default MRK Region is not configured"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "665997fcb0937a6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the AWS SDK Default Region MUST be used."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "25a8b20098277cbd"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If an AWS SDK Default Region can not be obtained initialization MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "ee954da46534fa3f"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The key id list MUST be empty in discovery mode."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84729d0e7c8cea42",
                  "2eb4524869592b88"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The regional client supplier MUST be defined in discovery mode."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8aaa9dfe00d17d0a",
            "005917faeff76e97",
            "290a1f8b684c1e79",
            "2baaab08670dec9a",
            "2baaab08670dec9a",
            "21544912b120ab9e",
            "db11024267fe1cd4",
            "665997fcb0937a6b",
            "665997fcb0937a6b",
            "25a8b20098277cbd",
            "ee954da46534fa3f",
            "2eb4524869592b88"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "get-master-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "93ad4ffaa2f9fb75"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The input MUST be the same as the [Master Key Provider Get Master Key](../master-key-provider-interface.md#get-master-key) interface."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "cf14d4bf8fd85ab7"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The function MUST only provide master keys if the input provider id equals `aws-kms`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "201de3d78950ef32"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "In strict mode, the requested AWS KMS key ARN MUST match a member of the configured key ids"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "201de3d78950ef32"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "by using [AWS KMS MRK Match for Decrypt](aws-kms-mrk-match-for-decrypt.md#implementation)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "201de3d78950ef32"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "otherwise this function MUST error."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "46bf87b3da366c93"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "In discovery mode, the requested AWS KMS key identifier MUST be a well formed AWS KMS ARN."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "f100503e2f748779"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "In discovery mode if a discovery filter is configured"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "f100503e2f748779"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the requested AWS KMS key ARN’s `partition` MUST match the discovery filter’s `partition`"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "f100503e2f748779"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "and the AWS KMS key ARN’s `account` MUST exist in the discovery filter’s account id set."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "48a94caa0805db12"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If the requested AWS KMS key identifier is not a well formed ARN"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "48a94caa0805db12"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the AWS Region MUST be the configured default region this SHOULD be obtained from the AWS SDK."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "10032b3ec81bdfb8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Otherwise if the requested AWS KMS key identifier is [identified as a multi-Region key](aws-kms-key-arn.md#identifying-an-aws-kms-multi-region-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "10032b3ec81bdfb8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "then AWS Region MUST be the region from the AWS KMS key ARN stored in the provider info from the encrypted data key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "8aaa6d33b5b77a39"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Otherwise if the mode is discovery then the AWS Region MUST be the discovery MRK region."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "7ed84e9f09065e48"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Finally if the provider info is [identified as a multi-Region key](aws-kms-key-arn.md#identifying-an-aws-kms-multi-region-key)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "7ed84e9f09065e48"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the AWS Region MUST be the region from the AWS KMS key in the configured key ids matched to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "7ed84e9f09065e48"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the requested AWS KMS key by using [AWS KMS MRK Match for Decrypt](aws-kms-mrk-match-for-decrypt.md#implementation)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "33cfc800fdd96ef2"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "An AWS KMS client MUST be obtained by calling the regional client supplier with this AWS Region."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "96ee6d55ebbcbb68"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "In strict mode a [AWS KMS MRK Aware Master Key](aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key.md) MUST be returned configured with"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- The AWS KMS obtained by calling the regional client supplier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- The AWS KMS key in the configured key ids matched to the requested AWS KMS key by using [AWS KMS MRK Match for Decrypt](aws-kms-mrk-match-for-decrypt.md#implementation)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- The configured grant tokens."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "63c03ce6841d8091"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "In discovery mode a [AWS KMS MRK Aware Master Key](aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key.md) MUST be returned configured with"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- The AWS KMS obtained by calling the regional client supplier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- An AWS KMS key ARN where the `region` element is the AWS Region, and every other ARN element matches the requested AWS KMS key ARN."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- The configured grant tokens."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e94de0e067c17253",
                  "4c9a99271dcf1326"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The output MUST be the same as the [Master Key Provider Get Master Key](../master-key-provider-interface.md#get-master-key) interface."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "93ad4ffaa2f9fb75",
            "cf14d4bf8fd85ab7",
            "201de3d78950ef32",
            "201de3d78950ef32",
            "201de3d78950ef32",
            "46bf87b3da366c93",
            "f100503e2f748779",
            "f100503e2f748779",
            "f100503e2f748779",
            "48a94caa0805db12",
            "48a94caa0805db12",
            "10032b3ec81bdfb8",
            "10032b3ec81bdfb8",
            "8aaa6d33b5b77a39",
            "7ed84e9f09065e48",
            "7ed84e9f09065e48",
            "7ed84e9f09065e48",
            "33cfc800fdd96ef2",
            "96ee6d55ebbcbb68",
            "63c03ce6841d8091",
            "4c9a99271dcf1326"
          ],
          "title": "Get Master Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da535d3fd012f792",
                  "6687e538eafd1425"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The input MUST be the same as the [Master Key Provider Get Master Keys For Encryption](../master-key-provider-interface.md#get-master-keys-for-encryption) interface."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da535d3fd012f792",
                  "a2befc086d6a4d63"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If the configured mode is discovery the function MUST return an empty list."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da535d3fd012f792",
                  "30c7ca1dc156e55c"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If the configured mode is strict this function MUST return a list of master keys"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da535d3fd012f792",
                  "30c7ca1dc156e55c"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "obtained by calling [Get Master Key](aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key-provider.md#get-master-key) for each AWS KMS key identifier in the configured key ids"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da535d3fd012f792",
                  "d3833c1a54dd1984"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The output MUST be the same as the [Master Key Provider Get Master Keys For Encryption](../master-key-provider-interface.md#get-master-keys-for-encryption) interface."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6687e538eafd1425",
            "a2befc086d6a4d63",
            "30c7ca1dc156e55c",
            "30c7ca1dc156e55c",
            "d3833c1a54dd1984"
          ],
          "title": "Get Master Keys For Encryption"
        },
        {
          "id": "decrypt-data-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "890e5759bfae0a4e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The input MUST be the same as the [Master Key Provider Decrypt Data Key](../master-key-provider-interface.md#decrypt-data-key) interface."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "99cb87b63ca97b07"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The set of encrypted data keys MUST first be filtered to match this master key’s configuration."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "6aa52c2778561485"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "To match the encrypted data key’s provider ID MUST exactly match the value “aws-kms”."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "195bf283ef3e9f22"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Additionally each provider info MUST be a [valid AWS KMS ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn) with a resource type of `key`."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "baf06a2c4a7035d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "For each encrypted data key in the filtered set, one at a time,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "baf06a2c4a7035d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the master key provider MUST call [Get Master Key](aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key-provider.md#get-master-key)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "baf06a2c4a7035d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "with the encrypted data key’s provider info as the AWS KMS key ARN."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "fd7675723f4d75e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "It MUST call [Decrypt Data Key](aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key.md#decrypt-data-key) on this master key with the input algorithm,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "fd7675723f4d75e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "this single encrypted data key, and the input encryption context."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "edd7b20ed2bf3139"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If this attempt results in an error, then these errors MUST be collected."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "10f2bb02a63cce34"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If the decrypt data key call is successful, then this function MUST return this result"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "10f2bb02a63cce34"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "and not attempt to decrypt any more encrypted data keys."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "7ad03adbc1af6129"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If all the input encrypted data keys have been processed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "7ad03adbc1af6129"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "then this function MUST yield an error that includes all the collected errors."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bf32d59e24576d7f",
                  "ba4608c4fcf7dd17"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The output MUST be the same as the [Master Key Provider Decrypt Data Key](../master-key-provider-interface.md#decrypt-data-key) interface."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "890e5759bfae0a4e",
            "99cb87b63ca97b07",
            "6aa52c2778561485",
            "195bf283ef3e9f22",
            "baf06a2c4a7035d8",
            "baf06a2c4a7035d8",
            "baf06a2c4a7035d8",
            "fd7675723f4d75e7",
            "fd7675723f4d75e7",
            "edd7b20ed2bf3139",
            "10f2bb02a63cce34",
            "10f2bb02a63cce34",
            "7ad03adbc1af6129",
            "7ad03adbc1af6129",
            "ba4608c4fcf7dd17"
          ],
          "title": "Decrypt Data Key"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS MRK Aware Master Key Provider"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-mrk-aware-master-key",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS MRK Aware Master Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.2.2"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "A Master Key which interacts with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)",
            "to create, encrypt, and decrypt data keys",
            "using AWS KMS defined Customer Master Keys (CMKs)."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "interface",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ac35cac35d53fdc",
                  "8cc6f80bacc81ebb"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "MUST implement the [Master Key Interface](../master-key-interface.md#interface)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8cc6f80bacc81ebb"
          ],
          "title": "Interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8",
                  "1af8e30817763259"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "On initialization, the caller MUST provide:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- An AWS KMS key identifier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- An AWS KMS SDK client."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8",
                  "f674c718f9c2218c"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The AWS KMS key identifier MUST NOT be null or empty."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8",
                  "89f8743e73989496"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The AWS KMS key identifier MUST be [a valid identifier](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-identifier)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8",
                  "fb464a34f57d2a9d"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The AWS KMS SDK client MUST not be null."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8",
                  "84d6295d642057cb"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The master key MUST be able to be configured with an optional list of Grant Tokens."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dbe99d9e030f3fd8",
                  "7a0f202134472046"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "This configuration SHOULD be on initialization and SHOULD be immutable."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1af8e30817763259",
            "f674c718f9c2218c",
            "89f8743e73989496",
            "fb464a34f57d2a9d",
            "84d6295d642057cb",
            "7a0f202134472046"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "get-master-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "68aa4d0bc4405029",
                  "9389402b8e74bf5f"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "MUST be unchanged from the Master Key interface."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9389402b8e74bf5f"
          ],
          "title": "Get Master Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "get-master-keys-for-encryption",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a6d04f7315259a6",
                  "c6c0e2e8c8d0cb18"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "MUST be unchanged from the Master Key interface."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c6c0e2e8c8d0cb18"
          ],
          "title": "Get Master Keys For Encryption"
        },
        {
          "id": "decrypt-data-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "811ec3503f52cad0"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The inputs MUST be the same as the [Master Key Decrypt Data Key](../master-key-interface.md#decrypt-data-key) interface."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "b32860843b8fa9f9"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The set of encrypted data keys MUST first be filtered to match this master key’s configuration."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "79b12c162837d64a"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "To match the encrypted data key’s provider ID MUST exactly match the value “aws-kms”"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "79b12c162837d64a"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "and the the function [AWS KMS MRK Match for Decrypt](aws-kms-mrk-match-for-decrypt.md#implementation) called with the configured AWS KMS key identifier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "79b12c162837d64a"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "and the encrypted data key’s provider info MUST return `true`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "a5247e7077c41612"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Additionally each provider info MUST be a [valid AWS KMS ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn) with a resource type of `key`."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "b99f0796f569a72b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "For each encrypted data key in the filtered set, one at a time,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "b99f0796f569a72b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the master key MUST attempt to decrypt the data key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "5defbb31c375dee9"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If this attempt results in an error,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "5defbb31c375dee9"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "then these errors MUST be collected."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "b789bbfcf5fb530c"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "To decrypt the encrypted data key this master key MUST use the configured AWS KMS client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "b789bbfcf5fb530c"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "to make an [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `KeyId`: The configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `CiphertextBlob`: The `ciphertext` from the encrypted data key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `EncryptionContext`: The encryption context included in the input."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `GrantTokens`: The configured grant tokens."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "c632b4565932f2f8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If the call succeeds then the response’s `KeyId` MUST be equal to the configured AWS KMS key identifier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "c632b4565932f2f8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "otherwise the function MUST collect an error."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "199826aaf6baffc8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The response’s `Plaintext`’s length MUST equal the length required by the requested algorithm suite"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "199826aaf6baffc8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "otherwise the function MUST collect an error."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "dc6695b1031fa3fb"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If the AWS KMS response satisfies the requirements then it MUST be use and this function MUST return"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "dc6695b1031fa3fb"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "and not attempt to decrypt any more encrypted data keys."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "744fd6baaed4effa"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If all the input encrypted data keys have been processed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "744fd6baaed4effa"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "then this function MUST yield an error that includes all the collected errors."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6ce4d0bb03577a",
                  "1ec4c9b928243948"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The output MUST be the same as the [Master Key Decrypt Data Key](../master-key-interface.md#decrypt-data-key) interface."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "811ec3503f52cad0",
            "b32860843b8fa9f9",
            "79b12c162837d64a",
            "79b12c162837d64a",
            "79b12c162837d64a",
            "a5247e7077c41612",
            "b99f0796f569a72b",
            "b99f0796f569a72b",
            "5defbb31c375dee9",
            "5defbb31c375dee9",
            "b789bbfcf5fb530c",
            "b789bbfcf5fb530c",
            "c632b4565932f2f8",
            "c632b4565932f2f8",
            "199826aaf6baffc8",
            "199826aaf6baffc8",
            "dc6695b1031fa3fb",
            "dc6695b1031fa3fb",
            "744fd6baaed4effa",
            "744fd6baaed4effa",
            "1ec4c9b928243948"
          ],
          "title": "Decrypt Data Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "generate-data-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7",
                  "00e0ee813081f415"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The inputs MUST be the same as the [Master Key Generate Data Key](../master-key-interface.md#generate-data-key) interface."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7",
                  "e9b5898e3c04a410"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "This master key MUST use the configured AWS KMS client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7",
                  "e9b5898e3c04a410"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "to make an [AWS KMS GenerateDatakey](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_GenerateDataKey.html) request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `KeyId`: The configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `NumberOfBytes`: The key derivation input length specified by the algorithm suite included in the input."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `EncryptionContext`: The encryption context included in the input."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `GrantTokens`: The configured grant tokens."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7",
                  "2103e823feb691a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If the call succeeds the AWS KMS Generate Data Key response’s `Plaintext` MUST match the key derivation input length specified by the algorithm suite included in the input."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7",
                  "20b8e8f9bd77afe6"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The response’s `KeyId` MUST be valid."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7",
                  "e3d3ee34afedce2b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The response’s `Plaintext` MUST be the plaintext in the output."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7",
                  "ecadbcfa6e211af4"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The response’s cipher text blob MUST be used as the returned as the ciphertext for the encrypted data key in the output."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4a26c36ff850f7a7",
                  "130f3a51be6e3f9e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The output MUST be the same as the [Master Key Generate Data Key](../master-key-interface.md#generate-data-key) interface."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "00e0ee813081f415",
            "e9b5898e3c04a410",
            "e9b5898e3c04a410",
            "2103e823feb691a0",
            "20b8e8f9bd77afe6",
            "e3d3ee34afedce2b",
            "ecadbcfa6e211af4",
            "130f3a51be6e3f9e"
          ],
          "title": "Generate Data Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "encrypt-data-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e",
                  "dd0534d7e0e7a13a"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The inputs MUST be the same as the [Master Key Encrypt Data Key](../master-key-interface.md#encrypt-data-key) interface."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e",
                  "d22e3cac6b8c6503"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The master key MUST use the configured AWS KMS client to make an [AWS KMS Encrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Encrypt.html) request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `KeyId`: The configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `PlaintextDataKey`: The plaintext data key obtained from the input."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `EncryptionContext`: the encryption context included in the input."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "- `GrantTokens`: The configured grant tokens."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e",
                  "406e9f445dff35cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The AWS KMS Encrypt response MUST contain a valid `KeyId`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e",
                  "1b26d99927991bd6"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The response’s cipher text blob MUST be used as the `ciphertext` for the encrypted data key."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "924bc9a77f484b2e",
                  "d6a02bd121e21f27"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The output MUST be the same as the [Master Key Encrypt Data Key](../master-key-interface.md#encrypt-data-key) interface."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "dd0534d7e0e7a13a",
            "d22e3cac6b8c6503",
            "406e9f445dff35cc",
            "1b26d99927991bd6",
            "d6a02bd121e21f27"
          ],
          "title": "Encrypt Data Key"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS MRK Aware Master Key"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-mrk-discovery-keyring.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-mrk-discovery-keyring",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS MRK Discovery Keyring"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.2.2"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "A keyring which interacts with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)",
            "to decrypt data keys using a filter to identify Customer Master Keys (CMKs)."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "interface",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7d23585a8378f430",
                  "2bdbee618ad10efd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST implement that [AWS Encryption SDK Keyring interface](../keyring-interface.md#interface)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2bdbee618ad10efd"
          ],
          "title": "Interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "adc5f33f3713a826",
                  "01002ca64d2a27dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "On initialization the keyring MUST accept the following parameters:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- A required AWS KMS client",
            "- A required string indicating the region of the KMS client",
            "- An optional discovery filter that is an AWS partition and a set of AWS accounts",
            "- An optional list of AWS KMS grant tokens",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e1fde33c966822ef",
                  "0b6bd84631cb8f36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "They keyring MUST fail initialization if any required parameters are missing or null."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65b40cfe34de7e11",
                  "27635580dbf48cf8"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "The keyring SHOULD fail initialization if the provided region does not match the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65b40cfe34de7e11",
                  "27635580dbf48cf8"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "region of the KMS client."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " Note that in some implementations this may not be"
              }
            ],
            "possible, as some AWS SDKs may not provide an API to access this information."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "01002ca64d2a27dd",
            "0b6bd84631cb8f36",
            "27635580dbf48cf8",
            "27635580dbf48cf8"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "onencrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d97a3674a63644a3",
                  "53a038666ec6b872"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This function MUST fail."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "53a038666ec6b872"
          ],
          "title": "OnEncrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "ondecrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cee4693a841ac659",
                  "e7f55c7adc87585e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST take [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cee4693a841ac659",
                  "e7f55c7adc87585e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "a list of [encrypted data keys](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "090b6c8423f76311",
                  "27fd545daacf553b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) already contained a valid plaintext data key,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "090b6c8423f76311",
                  "27fd545daacf553b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "they keyring MUST fail and MUST NOT modify the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f9eae5bdc9898d7e",
                  "ad629830aec05e55"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The set of encrypted data keys MUST first be filtered to match this keyring’s configuration."
              }
            ],
            "For the encrypted data key to match",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a219576d116216e",
                  "1fab850b179209bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- Its provider ID MUST exactly match the value “aws-kms”."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df0ddf72df62246b",
                  "aa9cedcb7002a6fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The provider info MUST be a [valid AWS KMS ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn) with a resource type of `key` or OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "488969bf6c1e050d",
                  "86fabbc044163251"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- If a discovery filter is configured, its partition and the provider info partition MUST match."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ddace42f081d86d3",
                  "68d550bc217a8324"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- If a discovery filter is configured, its set of accounts MUST contain the provider info account."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec82e9a8266da9b4",
                  "b90a8791eca393be"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- If the provider info is not [identified as a multi-Region key](aws-kms-key-arn.md#identifying-an-aws-kms-multi-region-key), then the provider info’s Region MUST match the AWS KMS client region."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c51bdcbacbb66706",
                  "5b4b8d77f8949702"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "For each encrypted data key in the filtered set, one at a time, the OnDecrypt MUST attempt to decrypt the data key."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " If this attempt results in an error, then these errors are collected."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd0532c06b6cfae6",
                  "d926403cb07c6154"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "To attempt to decrypt a particular [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd0532c06b6cfae6",
                  "d926403cb07c6154"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST call [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) with the configured AWS KMS client."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2ea91a346dff7d6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "When calling [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html), the keyring MUST call with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d282987031afd7a",
                  "7ff41b42ee796ca9"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- `KeyId`: If the provider info’s resource type is `key` and its resource is a multi-Region key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d282987031afd7a",
                  "7ff41b42ee796ca9"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "then a new ARN MUST be created where the region part MUST equal the AWS KMS client region"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d282987031afd7a",
                  "7ff41b42ee796ca9"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "and every other part MUST equal the provider info."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a8346c25ff1b35ec",
                  "823c0c877c11fa31"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Otherwise it MUST be the provider info."
              }
            ],
            "- `CiphertextBlob`: The [encrypted data key ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext).",
            "- `EncryptionContext`: The [encryption context](../structures.md#encryption-context) included in the input [decryption materials](structures.md#decryption-materials).",
            "- `GrantTokens`: this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)",
            "",
            "If the call to [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) succeeds OnDecrypt verifies",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ebbe3bf98d348208"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The `KeyId` field in the response MUST equal the requested `KeyId`"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5529b3d0405659fe",
                  "184abca8b5a1b6c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- The length of the response’s `Plaintext` MUST equal the [key derivation input length](../algorithm-suites.md#key-derivation-input-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5529b3d0405659fe",
                  "184abca8b5a1b6c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "specified by the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md) included in the input [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e683e673b57aa2b1",
                  "c3259714383f2850"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the response does not satisfies these requirements"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e683e673b57aa2b1",
                  "c3259714383f2850"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "then an error is collected and the next encrypted data key in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f6a797c85f181aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Since the response does satisfies these requirements"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f6a797c85f181aa"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "then OnDecrypt MUST do the following with the response:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- set the plaintext data key on the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) as the response `Plaintext`.",
            "- immediately return the modified [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f95af6a4a2709718",
                  "3f59752fc1ef4a5c"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If OnDecrypt fails to successfully decrypt any [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f95af6a4a2709718",
                  "3f59752fc1ef4a5c"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "then it MUST yield an error that includes all collected errors."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e7f55c7adc87585e",
            "e7f55c7adc87585e",
            "27fd545daacf553b",
            "27fd545daacf553b",
            "ad629830aec05e55",
            "1fab850b179209bc",
            "aa9cedcb7002a6fa",
            "86fabbc044163251",
            "68d550bc217a8324",
            "b90a8791eca393be",
            "5b4b8d77f8949702",
            "d926403cb07c6154",
            "d926403cb07c6154",
            "d2ea91a346dff7d6",
            "7ff41b42ee796ca9",
            "7ff41b42ee796ca9",
            "7ff41b42ee796ca9",
            "823c0c877c11fa31",
            "ebbe3bf98d348208",
            "184abca8b5a1b6c3",
            "184abca8b5a1b6c3",
            "c3259714383f2850",
            "c3259714383f2850",
            "9f6a797c85f181aa",
            "9f6a797c85f181aa",
            "3f59752fc1ef4a5c",
            "3f59752fc1ef4a5c"
          ],
          "title": "OnDecrypt"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS MRK Discovery Keyring"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-mrk-keyring.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-mrk-keyring",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS MRK Keyring"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.2.2"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "A keyring which interacts with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)",
            "to create, encrypt, and decrypt data keys",
            "using AWS KMS defined Customer Master Keys (CMKs)."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "interface",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9fc204f20c73777d",
                  "ae2fc5b8927f8ca9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST implement the [AWS Encryption SDK Keyring interface](../keyring-interface.md#interface)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "ae2fc5b8927f8ca9"
          ],
          "title": "Interface"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aaf5dc9723cca4a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "On initialization the caller MUST provide:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- An AWS KMS key identifier",
            "- An AWS KMS SDK client",
            "- An optional list of Grant Tokens",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1ee408e80275075",
                  "d8e54db7336911ec"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The AWS KMS key identifier MUST NOT be null or empty."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1ee408e80275075",
                  "c4ea955d5b22ff7e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The AWS KMS key identifier MUST be [a valid identifier](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-identifier)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1a0ee0198b665a9",
                  "7b9ab375e49a8fe3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The AWS KMS SDK client MUST NOT be null."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "aaf5dc9723cca4a7",
            "d8e54db7336911ec",
            "c4ea955d5b22ff7e",
            "7b9ab375e49a8fe3"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "onencrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d6a14ae34a7816d4",
                  "36e2f8b79cd470f6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST take [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bb5cea42bc894575",
                  "6024d5c91aa1e65f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) do not contain a plaintext data key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bb5cea42bc894575",
                  "6024d5c91aa1e65f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST attempt to generate a new plaintext data key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bb5cea42bc894575",
                  "6024d5c91aa1e65f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "by calling [AWS KMS GenerateDataKey](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_GenerateDataKey.html)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5aad81e97dccbc7e",
                  "82a920001ed46f77"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the keyring calls AWS KMS GenerateDataKeys,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5aad81e97dccbc7e",
                  "82a920001ed46f77"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "it MUST use the configured AWS KMS client to make the call."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "965f9f189a981197",
                  "aa0ea02c42edc8e1"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The keyring MUST call AWS KMS GenerateDataKeys with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- `KeyId`: this keyring's KMS key identifier.",
            "- `NumberOfBytes`: the [key derivation input length](../algorithm-suites.md#key-derivation-input-length)",
            "  specified by the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md) included in the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials).",
            "- `EncryptionContext`: the [encryption context](../structures.md#encryption-context)",
            "  included in the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials).",
            "- `GrantTokens`: this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f481f044db40ad76",
                  "e6cca36cc0243ea0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the call to [AWS KMS GenerateDataKey](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_GenerateDataKey.html) does not succeed,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f481f044db40ad76",
                  "e6cca36cc0243ea0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST NOT modify the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) and MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b7a6d93d287d1f3",
                  "9c62a77f2866fe91"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the Generate Data Key call succeeds, OnEncrypt MUST verify that the response `Plaintext` length matches"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b7a6d93d287d1f3",
                  "9c62a77f2866fe91"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "the specification of the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md)'s Key Derivation Input Length field."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0257d0c9b21c0836",
                  "040968b9c594ab62"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The Generate Data Key response’s `KeyId` MUST be [A valid AWS KMS key ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#identifying-an-aws-kms-multi-region-key)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "73aef8efb22b4c0c",
                  "28ae35a1eb8fa673"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If verified, OnEncrypt MUST do the following with the response from [AWS KMS GenerateDataKey](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_GenerateDataKey.html):"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- set the plaintext data key on the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) as the response `Plaintext`.",
            "",
            "- append a new [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) to the encrypted data key list in the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials), constructed as follows:",
            "",
            "  - the [ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext) is the response `CiphertextBlob`.",
            "  - the [key provider id](../structures.md#key-provider-id) is \"aws-kms\".",
            "  - the [key provider information](../structures.md#key-provider-information) is the response `KeyId`.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d7238accb7e15634",
                  "b5ec07b0d0599559"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- OnEncrypt MUST output the modified [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "02172a4ac3d3a0a7",
                  "a046180f4ec63c5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials) do contain a plaintext data key,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "02172a4ac3d3a0a7",
                  "a046180f4ec63c5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnEncrypt MUST attempt to encrypt the plaintext data key using the configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "91f52d95f51f1c53",
                  "5f994a0f79d0d084"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The keyring MUST call [AWS KMS Encrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Encrypt.html) using the configured AWS KMS client."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "77c504da1b0c1df1",
                  "5afb52fbfbd2ba36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The keyring MUST AWS KMS Encrypt call with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- `KeyId`: The configured AWS KMS key identifier.",
            "- `PlaintextDataKey`: the plaintext data key in the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials).",
            "- `EncryptionContext`: the [encryption context](../structures.md#encryption-context) included in the input [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials).",
            "",
            "- `GrantTokens`: this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1dc3cd56590e22df",
                  "e2c9d90c7eb7d745"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the call to [AWS KMS Encrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Encrypt.html) does not succeed, OnEncrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d00ab36fa1d8f473",
                  "55c782ea6bf641bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the Encrypt call succeeds the response’s `KeyId` MUST be [A valid AWS KMS key ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6455837cd98ce099",
                  "b65cc50b678f4b8e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If verified, OnEncrypt MUST do the following with the response from [AWS KMS Encrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Encrypt.html):"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- append a new [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) to the encrypted data key list in the [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials), constructed as follows:",
            "",
            "  - The [ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext) is the response `CiphertextBlob`.",
            "  - The [key provider id](../structures.md#key-provider-id) is \"aws-kms\".",
            "  - The [key provider information](../structures.md#key-provider-information) is the response `KeyId`. Note that the `KeyId` in the response is always in key ARN format.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c01422738335f014",
                  "51d90b0886757a9d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If all Encrypt calls succeed, OnEncrypt MUST output the modified [encryption materials](../structures.md#encryption-materials)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "36e2f8b79cd470f6",
            "6024d5c91aa1e65f",
            "6024d5c91aa1e65f",
            "6024d5c91aa1e65f",
            "82a920001ed46f77",
            "82a920001ed46f77",
            "aa0ea02c42edc8e1",
            "e6cca36cc0243ea0",
            "e6cca36cc0243ea0",
            "9c62a77f2866fe91",
            "9c62a77f2866fe91",
            "040968b9c594ab62",
            "28ae35a1eb8fa673",
            "b5ec07b0d0599559",
            "a046180f4ec63c5a",
            "a046180f4ec63c5a",
            "5f994a0f79d0d084",
            "5afb52fbfbd2ba36",
            "e2c9d90c7eb7d745",
            "55c782ea6bf641bf",
            "b65cc50b678f4b8e",
            "51d90b0886757a9d"
          ],
          "title": "OnEncrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "ondecrypt",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6ea27b80336af73",
                  "3620223782ab6354"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST take [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6ea27b80336af73",
                  "3620223782ab6354"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "a list of [encrypted data keys](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key) as input."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2284d77cc4657e94"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) already contained a valid plaintext data key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2284d77cc4657e94"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST immediately return the unmodified [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a2d33c8e984b8501",
                  "9b6c95df0f112c20"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "The set of encrypted data keys MUST first be filtered to match this keyring’s configuration."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " For the encrypted data key to match"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "00a54a5b123fbeb4",
                  "21d743f5f330d026"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- Its provider ID MUST exactly match the value “aws-kms”."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7fa7527c1b08816e",
                  "f918252fd45451a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The provider info MUST be a [valid AWS KMS ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn) with a resource type of `key` or OnDecrypt MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84f3e2ef2b4f51c1",
                  "12625d5d45d85b68"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "- The the function [AWS KMS MRK Match for Decrypt](aws-kms-mrk-match-for-decrypt.md#implementation)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "84f3e2ef2b4f51c1",
                  "12625d5d45d85b68"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "called with the configured AWS KMS key identifier and the provider info MUST return `true`."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df6a89cbcfd31b50",
                  "a638205c3d0dad3b"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "For each encrypted data key in the filtered set, one at a time, the OnDecrypt MUST attempt to decrypt the data key."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "df6a89cbcfd31b50",
                  "14a376e18a63a376"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If this attempt results in an error, then these errors MUST be collected."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b2b26e34a333d4fd",
                  "f733a131575d3134"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "To attempt to decrypt a particular [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b2b26e34a333d4fd",
                  "f733a131575d3134"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "OnDecrypt MUST call [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) with the configured AWS KMS client."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67827a583e759731",
                  "24230e6db9a0b491"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "When calling [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html), the keyring MUST call with a request constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- `KeyId`: The configured AWS KMS key identifier.",
            "- `CiphertextBlob`: the [encrypted data key ciphertext](../structures.md#ciphertext).",
            "- `EncryptionContext`: the [encryption context](../structures.md#encryption-context) included in the input [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials).",
            "",
            "- `GrantTokens`: this keyring's [grant tokens](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#grant_token)",
            "",
            "If the call to [AWS KMS Decrypt](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_Decrypt.html) succeeds OnDecrypt verifies",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "81261e4dee6e6695",
                  "f02a152bf9a1a344"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- The `KeyId` field in the response MUST equal the configured AWS KMS key identifier."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cbf3c84636edca01",
                  "349b2ca9bc47682a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "- The length of the response’s `Plaintext` MUST equal the [key derivation input length](../algorithm-suites.md#key-derivation-input-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cbf3c84636edca01",
                  "349b2ca9bc47682a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "specified by the [algorithm suite](../algorithm-suites.md) included in the input [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "375a9d4e584443ee",
                  "5a3d6348c6ee3340"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the response does not satisfies these requirements then an error MUST be collected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "375a9d4e584443ee",
                  "5a3d6348c6ee3340"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "and the next encrypted data key in the filtered set MUST be attempted."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6190eb1bc2fc6f4e"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the response does satisfies these requirements then OnDecrypt MUST do the following with the response:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- set the plaintext data key on the [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials) as the response `Plaintext`.",
            "- immediately return the modified [decryption materials](../structures.md#decryption-materials).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9c43437f15afad78"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If OnDecrypt fails to successfully decrypt any [encrypted data key](../structures.md#encrypted-data-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9c43437f15afad78"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "then it MUST yield an error that includes all the collected errors."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "3620223782ab6354",
            "3620223782ab6354",
            "2284d77cc4657e94",
            "2284d77cc4657e94",
            "9b6c95df0f112c20",
            "21d743f5f330d026",
            "f918252fd45451a7",
            "12625d5d45d85b68",
            "12625d5d45d85b68",
            "a638205c3d0dad3b",
            "14a376e18a63a376",
            "f733a131575d3134",
            "f733a131575d3134",
            "24230e6db9a0b491",
            "f02a152bf9a1a344",
            "349b2ca9bc47682a",
            "349b2ca9bc47682a",
            "5a3d6348c6ee3340",
            "5a3d6348c6ee3340",
            "6190eb1bc2fc6f4e",
            "9c43437f15afad78",
            "9c43437f15afad78"
          ],
          "title": "OnDecrypt"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS MRK Keyring"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-mrk-match-for-decrypt.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-mrk-match-for-decrypt",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS MRK Match for Decrypt"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.2.2"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "Since the AWS Encryption SDK stores the AWS KMS key ARN",
            "in the encrypted data key of the message format",
            "an AWS KMS component needs to be able to evaluate",
            "if a configured ARN matches a stored ARN.",
            "This is especially important for multi-Region keys because the match does not need to be exact."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementation",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "27bf48414c5b2da9",
                  "1150d9e2f6063717"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The caller MUST provide:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "27bf48414c5b2da9"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- 2 AWS KMS key identifiers"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8bd161d5182175ad",
                  "8be4c49038360c24"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If both identifiers are identical, this function MUST return `true`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f2ed59433066c85",
                  "3313fcfb5bdd96be"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Otherwise if either input is not [identified as a multi-Region key](aws-kms-key-arn.md#identifying-an-aws-kms-multi-region-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f2ed59433066c85",
                  "3313fcfb5bdd96be"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "then this function MUST return `false`."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fb05c55c20774d26",
                  "07a37bc8c2746b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Otherwise if both inputs are [identified as a multi-Region keys](aws-kms-key-arn.md#identifying-an-aws-kms-multi-region-key),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fb05c55c20774d26",
                  "07a37bc8c2746b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this function MUST return the result of comparing"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fb05c55c20774d26",
                  "07a37bc8c2746b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the `partition`, `service`, `accountId`, `resourceType`, and `resource` parts of both ARN inputs."
              }
            ],
            "NOTE: The `region` part is intentionally omitted."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1150d9e2f6063717",
            "8be4c49038360c24",
            "3313fcfb5bdd96be",
            "3313fcfb5bdd96be",
            "07a37bc8c2746b36",
            "07a37bc8c2746b36",
            "07a37bc8c2746b36"
          ],
          "title": "Implementation"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS MRK Match for Decrypt"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-mrk-multi-keyrings.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-mrk-multi-keyrings",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "AWS KMS MRK Multi Keyrings"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.2.2"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.2.2",
            "",
            "  - Initial record"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "The AWS KMS MRK keyrings only operate on a single AWS KMS key ARN.",
            "However customers want to easily configure multiple AWS KMS key ARNs.",
            "These functions compose multiple AWS KMS key ARNs and return a single Multi Keyring."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119).",
            "",
            "Customers need a way to compose the single AWS KMS keyrings in an easy way. These functions take configuration and produce and compose many keyrings into a Multi Keyring."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-mrk-multi-keyring",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "16ab290b220d3546"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The caller MUST provide:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- An optional AWS KMS key identifiers to use as the generator.",
            "- An optional set of AWS KMS key identifiers to us as child keyrings.",
            "- An optional method that can take a region string and return an AWS KMS client e.g. a regional client supplier",
            "- An optional list of AWS KMS grant tokens",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72b4f5af9007d00e",
                  "3f064afe3822a687"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If any of the AWS KMS key identifiers is not a [valid AWS KMS key ARN](aws-kms-key-arn.md#a-valid-aws-kms-arn), this function MUST fail"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72b4f5af9007d00e",
                  "311b7b26b0a93cb1",
                  "3f064afe3822a687"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "All AWS KMS identifiers are passed to [Assert AWS KMS MRK are unique](aws-kms-mrk-are-unique.md#Implementation)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72b4f5af9007d00e",
                  "311b7b26b0a93cb1",
                  "3f064afe3822a687"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "and the function MUST return success otherwise this MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6441d656af7eff6d",
                  "2c75c912b1092d1d",
                  "174cf84a36017916"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If a regional client supplier is not passed, then a default MUST be created that takes a region string and generates a default AWS SDK client for the given region."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "53f24dd1af2e6c53",
                  "3765002c67d82b78"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If there is a generator input then the generator keyring MUST be a [AWS KMS MRK Keyring](aws-kms-mrk-keyring.md) initialized with"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- The generator input.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33b8e5c26c077d29"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The AWS KMS client that MUST be created by the regional client supplier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33b8e5c26c077d29"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "when called with the region part of the generator ARN"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33b8e5c26c077d29"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "or a signal for the AWS SDK to select the default region."
              }
            ],
            "- The input list of AWS KMS grant tokens",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "36d3bedd7c45fc13",
                  "03fbd721874d6e54"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If there is a set of child identifiers then a set of [AWS KMS MRK Keyring](aws-kms-mrk-keyring.md) MUST be created for each AWS KMS key identifier by initialized each keyring with"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- AWS KMS key identifier.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0bbbc953ed543f02"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The AWS KMS client that MUST be created by the regional client supplier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0bbbc953ed543f02"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "when called with the region part of the AWS KMS key identifier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0bbbc953ed543f02"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "or a signal for the AWS SDK to select the default region."
              }
            ],
            "- The input list of AWS KMS grant tokens",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9030cd026515aebb",
                  "c59ef37f5894b755"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "NOTE: The AWS Encryption SDK SHOULD NOT attempt to evaluate its own default region."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "054c5a9b9ec3f5fd",
                  "cdbf91707e0c77e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Then a [Multi-Keyring](../multi-keyring.md#inputs) MUST be initialize by using this generator keyring as the [generator keyring](../multi-keyring.md#generator-keyring) and this set of child keyrings as the [child keyrings](../multi-keyring.md#child-keyrings)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "054c5a9b9ec3f5fd",
                  "626eb5c0baa54eb4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This Multi-Keyring MUST be this functions output."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "16ab290b220d3546",
            "3f064afe3822a687",
            "3f064afe3822a687",
            "3f064afe3822a687",
            "174cf84a36017916",
            "3765002c67d82b78",
            "33b8e5c26c077d29",
            "33b8e5c26c077d29",
            "33b8e5c26c077d29",
            "03fbd721874d6e54",
            "0bbbc953ed543f02",
            "0bbbc953ed543f02",
            "0bbbc953ed543f02",
            "c59ef37f5894b755",
            "cdbf91707e0c77e2",
            "626eb5c0baa54eb4"
          ],
          "title": "AWS KMS MRK Multi-Keyring"
        },
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-mrk-discovery-multi-keyring",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ea02efda8da413",
                  "d9fefee464096403"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The caller MUST provide:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ea02efda8da413"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- A set of Region strings"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ea02efda8da413"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- An optional discovery filter that is an AWS partition and a set of AWS accounts"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ea02efda8da413"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- An optional method that can take a region string and return an AWS KMS client e.g. a regional client supplier"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "26ea02efda8da413"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- An optional list of AWS KMS grant tokens"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2bd953dda9e834d",
                  "514adb9d7fb928bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If an empty set of Region is provided this function MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "959e02591800cad9",
                  "de1a6d80a43aab7a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If any element of the set of regions is null or an empty string this function MUST fail."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1714da4e090e12eb"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If a regional client supplier is not passed, then a default MUST be created that takes a region string and generates a default AWS SDK client for the given region."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c87eb69c0845935c",
                  "749558bb95332608"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "A set of AWS KMS clients MUST be created by calling regional client supplier for each region in the input set of regions."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50960e871f441596",
                  "2e540a7d7c5ed7b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Then a set of [AWS KMS MRK Discovery Keyring](aws-kms-mrk-discovery-keyring.md) MUST be created for each AWS KMS client by initializing each keyring with"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50960e871f441596"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- The AWS KMS client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50960e871f441596"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- The input discovery filter"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50960e871f441596"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- The input AWS KMS grant tokens"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "119ef257df8ca81f",
                  "da3cf6bdedb497d3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Then a [Multi-Keyring](../multi-keyring.md#inputs) MUST be initialize by using this set of discovery keyrings as the [child keyrings](../multi-keyring.md#child-keyrings)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "119ef257df8ca81f",
                  "6b1f0f790614f7e5"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This Multi-Keyring MUST be this functions output."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "d9fefee464096403",
            "514adb9d7fb928bc",
            "de1a6d80a43aab7a",
            "1714da4e090e12eb",
            "749558bb95332608",
            "2e540a7d7c5ed7b2",
            "da3cf6bdedb497d3",
            "6b1f0f790614f7e5"
          ],
          "title": "AWS KMS MRK Discovery Multi-Keyring"
        }
      ],
      "title": "AWS KMS MRK Multi Keyrings"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/aws-kms/aws-kms-multi-keyrings.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "aws-kms-multi-keyrings",
