            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "structure-3",
          "lines": [
            "Branch Key materials are a structure containing materials that are used to establish a key hierarchy in order to",
            "reuse a data key that wraps other data keys.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ce98aa04ecf385a",
                  "b53e2bc565ad867b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This structure MUST include all of the following fields:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ce98aa04ecf385a"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- [Branch Key](#branch-key)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ce98aa04ecf385a"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- [Branch Key Id](#branch-key-id)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ce98aa04ecf385a"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- [Branch Key Version](#branch-key-version)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6ce98aa04ecf385a"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- [Encryption Context](#encryption-context-3)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b53e2bc565ad867b"
          ],
          "title": "Structure"
        },
        {
          "id": "branch-key",
          "lines": [
            "Data keys that are reused to derive unique data keys for envelope encryption.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d1e9efbfc9762a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This data key MUST only be generated through"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d1e9efbfc9762a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "AWS KMS using the [`GenerateDataKeyWithoutPlaintext`](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_GenerateDataKeyWithoutPlaintext.html) API."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30cf12e0dbeac41d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This key MUST be 32 bytes long."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1d1e9efbfc9762a6",
            "1d1e9efbfc9762a6",
            "30cf12e0dbeac41d"
          ],
          "title": "Branch Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "branch-key-id",
          "lines": [
            "The UTF8 Encoded value of the ID of the corresponding [branch key](#branch-key).",
            "The plaintext value of which is stored in the [branch key store](./branch-key-store.md)."
          ],
          "title": "Branch Key Id"
        },
        {
          "id": "branch-key-version",
          "lines": [
            "The UTF8 Encoded value of the version of the corresponding [branch key](#branch-key).",
            "The plaintext value of which is stored in the [branch key store](./branch-key-store.md).",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c615e41412f9ce79"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "This value MUST be a version 4 [UUID](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc4122.txt)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c615e41412f9ce79"
          ],
          "title": "Branch Key Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "encryption-context-3",
          "lines": [
            "The [custom encryption context](#encryption-context) associated with this branch key."
          ],
          "title": "Encryption Context"
        },
        {
          "id": "beacon-key-materials",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Beacon Key Materials"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations-5",
          "lines": [
            "| Language | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation |",
            "| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------- |"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "structure-4",
          "lines": [
            "Beacon Key materials are a structure containing materials",
            "that are used in structured encryption.",
            "They contain HMAC keys derived from a Beacon Key",
            "stored in the [Keystore](branch-key-store.md)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4b075381f20db2d",
                  "205d82326f6f4425"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This structure MUST include the following fields:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4b075381f20db2d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- [Beacon Key Id](#beacon-key-id)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4b075381f20db2d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- [Encryption Context](#encryption-context-4)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0ba42bb2fe5fbde9",
                  "caf974261cf40d0f"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "This structure MAY include the following fields:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0ba42bb2fe5fbde9"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- [Beacon Key](#beacon-key)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0ba42bb2fe5fbde9"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "- [HMAC Keys](#hmac-keys)"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "205d82326f6f4425",
            "caf974261cf40d0f"
          ],
          "title": "Structure"
        },
        {
          "id": "beacon-key",
          "lines": [
            "The Beacon Key that is stored",
            "in the [Keystore](branch-key-store.md).",
            "",
            "The beacon key is optional,",
            "because the beacon key is used to derive [HMAC Keys](#hmac-keys).",
            "Once this has been complete,",
            "the beacon key can be discarded."
          ],
          "title": "Beacon Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "encryption-context-4",
          "lines": [
            "The [custom encryption context](#encryption-context) associated with this beacon key."
          ],
          "title": "Encryption Context"
        },
        {
          "id": "beacon-key-id",
          "lines": [
            "The Beacon key id that was used to obtain",
            "the beacon key from a [Keystore](branch-key-store.md)"
          ],
          "title": "Beacon Key Id"
        },
        {
          "id": "hmac-keys",
          "lines": [
            "A key-value mapping of arbitrary strings",
            "to bytes.",
            "Where the string is the name of the beacon and",
            "the bytes are the HMAC Key derived from the beacon key",
            "concatenated with the UTF8 Encoding of the beacon name."
          ],
          "title": "HMAC Keys"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Structures"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/synchronized-local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "synchronized-local-cryptographic-materials-cache",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Synchronized Local Cryptographic Materials Cache"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "changelog",
          "lines": [
            "- 0.1.0",
            "  - Initial record",
            "  - [Thread Safe Cache](../changes/2023-06-19_thread_safe_cache/change.md)"
          ],
          "title": "Changelog"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "The synchronized local Cryptographic Materials Cache (synchronized local CMC)",
            "is a built-in implementation of the [CMC interface](cryptographic-materials-cache.md)",
            "provided by the AWS Encryption SDK.",
            "",
            "It provides thread safe access to a [Local CMC](local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md)"
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "initialization",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c6ca319cc94e1f5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "On initialization of the synchronized local CMC,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c6ca319cc94e1f5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the caller MUST provide exactly what is required by a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c6ca319cc94e1f5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "[Local CMC](local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c6ca319cc94e1f5a",
            "c6ca319cc94e1f5a",
            "c6ca319cc94e1f5a"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "behaviors",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b2fac799e6e221b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "All behaviors MUST be exactly the same as a [Local CMC](local-cryptographic-materials-cache.md),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b2fac799e6e221b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "even if used in a multi-threaded context."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b2fac799e6e221b8",
            "b2fac799e6e221b8"
          ],
          "title": "Behaviors"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Synchronized Local Cryptographic Materials Cache"
    },
    "aws-encryption-sdk-specification/framework/transitive-requirements.md": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "transitive-requirements-for-supported-formats",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Transitive requirements for supported formats"
        },
        {
          "id": "version",
          "lines": [
            "0.1.0"
          ],
          "title": "Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "implementations",
          "lines": [
            "<!-- | Language   | Confirmed Compatible with Spec Version | Minimum Version Confirmed | Implementation                                                                                                                                            |",
            "| ---------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |",
            "| C          | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [cipher.c](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-c/blob/master/source/cipher.c)                                                                   |",
            "| NodeJS     | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [node_algorithms.ts](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-javascript/blob/master/modules/material-management/src/node_algorithms.ts)             |",
            "| Browser JS | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [web_crypto_algorithms.ts](https://github.com/awslabs/aws-encryption-sdk-javascript/blob/master/modules/material-management/src/web_crypto_algorithms.ts) |",
            "| Python     | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [identifiers.py](https://github.com/aws/aws-encryption-sdk-python/blob/master/src/aws_encryption_sdk/identifiers.py)                                      |",
            "| Java       | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [CryptoAlgorithm.java](https://github.com/aws/aws-encryption-sdk-java/blob/master/src/main/java/com/amazonaws/encryptionsdk/CryptoAlgorithm.java)         |",
            "| Java       | 0.1.0                                  | n/a                       | [AlgorithmSuites.dfy](https://github.com/aws/aws-encryption-sdk-dafny/blob/mainline/src/AwsCryptographicMaterialProviders/AlgorithmSuites.dfy)            | -->"
          ],
          "title": "Implementations"
        },
        {
          "id": "overview",
          "lines": [
            "There are implementation specific details that are relevant to some algorithm suites.",
            "These requirements may not be enforced by the Material Providers Library.",
            "This is the place to track these requirements.",
            "",
            "These requirements need to be ensured in the implementation of",
            "the encryption and decryption of each [supported format](./algorithm-suites.md#supported-format).",
            "By placing them in a separate markdown",
            "the expectation is that this file can be parsed by `duvet`",
            "and the appropriate annotations can be added in each library implementing a [supported format](./algorithm-suites.md#supported-formats)."
          ],
          "title": "Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "conventions-used-in-this-document",
          "lines": [
            "The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\"",
            "in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2119)."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions used in this document"
        },
        {
          "id": "hkdf-encryption-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe392e9360e6a6cb"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If an algorithm suite uses HKDF to derive the encryption key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe392e9360e6a6cb"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the AWS Encryption SDK MUST use HKDF with the following specifics:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "700c53f07fe8c507"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The hash function MUST be specified by the [algorithm suite key derivation settings](#algorithm-suites-encryption-key-derivation-settings)."
              }
            ],
            "- For the extract step:",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fd2c2b3d6316fcd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The input keying material MUST be the data key generated by the key provider."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3084821c518c7012"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The length of the input keying material MUST equal the [key derivation input length](#key-derivation-input-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3084821c518c7012"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "specified by the [algorithm suite encryption key derivation settings](#algorithm-suites-encryption-key-derivation-settings)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "857af0a7e5fc60e4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- If there is no salt length defined for the [algorithm suite encryption key derivation commitment setting](#algorithm-suites-encryption-key-derivation-settings),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "857af0a7e5fc60e4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the the salt MUST be a byte sequence of 0 as long as the hash length in bytes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90f3b149a720f176"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- If salt length is defined for the [algorithm suite encryption key derivation commitment setting](#algorithm-suites-encryption-key-derivation-settings),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90f3b149a720f176"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the salt MUST be the [message ID](../data-format/message-header.md#message-id) with a length equal to the salt length."
              }
            ],
            "- For the expand step:",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "852f0dbeaece8a87"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The input pseudorandom key MUST be the output from the extract step."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ea768516ab6763ba"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The length of the output keying material MUST equal the [encryption key length](#encryption-key-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ea768516ab6763ba"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "specified by the [algorithm suite encryption settings](#algorithm-suites-encryption-settings)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "639e9fe6c1c12668"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- If [key commitment](#key-commitment) for the [algorithm suite encryption key derivation setting](#algorithm-suites-encryption-key-derivation-settings) is True,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "639e9fe6c1c12668"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "then the input info MUST be a concatenation of the [algorithm suite ID](#algorithm-suite-id) followed by the string `DERIVEKEY` as UTF8 encoded bytes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f58cb2dec2c2e35"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- If [key commitment](#key-commitment) for the [algorithm suite encryption key derivation setting](#algorithm-suites-encryption-key-derivation-settings) is False,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f58cb2dec2c2e35"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the the input info MUST be a concatenation of the [algorithm suite ID](#algorithm-suite-id)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f58cb2dec2c2e35"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "followed by the [message ID](../data-format/message-header.md#message-id)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "fe392e9360e6a6cb",
            "fe392e9360e6a6cb",
            "700c53f07fe8c507",
            "fd2c2b3d6316fcd4",
            "3084821c518c7012",
            "3084821c518c7012",
            "857af0a7e5fc60e4",
            "857af0a7e5fc60e4",
            "90f3b149a720f176",
            "90f3b149a720f176",
            "852f0dbeaece8a87",
            "ea768516ab6763ba",
            "ea768516ab6763ba",
            "639e9fe6c1c12668",
            "639e9fe6c1c12668",
            "6f58cb2dec2c2e35",
            "6f58cb2dec2c2e35",
            "6f58cb2dec2c2e35"
          ],
          "title": "HKDF Encryption Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "hkdf-commit-key",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5feafdba15fd219f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If an algorithm suite uses HKDF to derive the commitment key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5feafdba15fd219f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the AWS Encryption SDK MUST use HKDF with the following specifics:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c1f1be72b5a0c1cb"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The hash function MUST be specified by the [algorithm suite commitment settings](#algorithm-suites-commit-key-derivation-settings)."
              }
            ],
            "- For the extract step:",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c79e994456106e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The input keying material MUST be the data key generated by the key provider."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72235a58df69c1be"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The length of the input keying material MUST equal the [key derivation input length](#key-derivation-input-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72235a58df69c1be"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "specified by the algorithm suite commit key derivation setting."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f00e2e95b23ab78"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The salt MUST be the [message ID](../data-format/message-header.md#message-id) with a length of 256 bits."
              }
            ],
            "- For the expand step:",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2ee6add9db53e5fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The input pseudorandom key MUST be the output from the extract step."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f0cf55b68fe9230d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The length of the output keying material MUST equal the [algorithm suite data length](#algorithm-suite-data-length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f0cf55b68fe9230d"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "specified by the [supported algorithm suites](#supported-algorithm-suites)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "473d0df5a33879e5"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "- The input info MUST the string `COMMITKEY` as UTF8 encoded bytes by the algorithm suite commitment settings."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "050b149e64e9ed33"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "For algorithm suites that support commitment,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "050b149e64e9ed33"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "the AWS Encryption SDK SHOULD only perform the extract step once"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "050b149e64e9ed33"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "and use the same output from the extract step"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "050b149e64e9ed33"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "for both the encryption key and the commitment key."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af4bd388d130a5c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Verification of the commitment key MUST be a constant time comparison."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "5feafdba15fd219f",
            "5feafdba15fd219f",
            "c1f1be72b5a0c1cb",
            "3c79e994456106e8",
            "72235a58df69c1be",
            "72235a58df69c1be",
            "3f00e2e95b23ab78",
            "2ee6add9db53e5fa",
            "f0cf55b68fe9230d",
            "f0cf55b68fe9230d",
            "473d0df5a33879e5",
            "050b149e64e9ed33",
            "050b149e64e9ed33",
            "050b149e64e9ed33",
            "050b149e64e9ed33",
            "af4bd388d130a5c9"
          ],
          "title": "HKDF Commit Key"
        },
        {
          "id": "ecdsa",
          "lines": [
            "Specification: ANS X9.62-2005",
            "(Not available publicly, but the specification for ECDSA is replicated in [SEC 1 version 2.0](https://www.secg.org/sec1-v2.pdf).",
            "Information about obtaining copies of ANS X9.62 is available at http://www.x9.org.)",
            "",
            "The Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA) is a signature algorithm.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90d86ede7ef8a862"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If specified to use ECDSA, the AWS Encryption SDK MUST use ECDSA with the following specifics:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "- The elliptic curve is specified by the algorithm suite.",
            "  The specific curves are defined in",
            "  [Digital Signature Standard (DSS) (FIPS PUB 186-4)](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.186-4.pdf).",
            "- The hash function is specified by the algorithm suite.",
            "- When included in the [message](../data-format/message.md), the output signature value is encoded using the",
            "  ANS.1 structure `ECDSA-Sig-Value` defined in section C.5 of [Sec 1 version 2.0](http://www.secg.org/sec1-v2.pdf):",
            "",
            "```",
            "ECDSA-Sig-Value ::= SEQUENCE {",
            "    r INTEGER,",
            "    s INTEGER",
            "}",
            "```",
            "",
            "- If serialized, the binary form of the verification key is equal to the elliptic curve point Q compressed",
            "  according to section 2.3.3 of [SEC 1 version 2.0](http://www.secg.org/sec1-v2.pdf)."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "90d86ede7ef8a862"
          ],
          "title": "ECDSA"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Transitive requirements for supported formats"
    }
  },
